1
00:00:06,589 --> 00:00:07,465
"Kian's B&B."

2
00:00:08,383 --> 00:00:09,968
I feel like I'm in a fairy tale.

3
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:12,012
This is incredible.

4
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:19,602
DEX IS HERE

5
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:24,899
Want to go sledding?

6
00:00:24,983 --> 00:00:25,817
MEANWHILE

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:26,943
It looked fun.

8
00:00:27,026 --> 00:00:28,737
-Let's go sledding.
-That sounds fun.

9
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,363
Want to go skating?

10
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:32,115
-We can skate for real?
-We can.

11
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:34,075
KIAN'S B&B

12
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:36,411
KIAN GOES OUT FIRST

13
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:38,038
AND THE REST FOLLOW

14
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:40,957
Let's go

15
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:43,501
Let's go sledding

16
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:45,503
ALL AT ONCE

17
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:48,715
They're doing something over there.

18
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:54,179
HAPPY

19
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:55,221
He's adorable.

20
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,348
They're sledding.

21
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:02,979
How am I supposed to join them?

22
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:06,733
COVERING HIS FACE WITH AN UMBRELLA

23
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:10,236
HE APPROACHES WALKING SIDEWAYS

24
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:13,490
I don't think they recognize me yet.

25
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:14,991
TOO PREOCCUPIED WITH SLEDDING

26
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:16,076
He went far.

27
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,702
NOW HE'S RIGHT IN FRONT OF THEM

28
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:22,457
Hello! I'm here to work part-time!

29
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:24,292
Hello!

30
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:26,753
PART-TIME WORKER DEX

31
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:28,630
-What? No way.
-I don't believe it.

32
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:29,798
A PART-TIME WORKER IS HERE?

33
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:32,175
GENUINELY SURPRISED

34
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:33,301
Hello.

35
00:01:34,552 --> 00:01:37,138
I was happy. We'd gotten so many guests,

36
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:38,848
so we really needed a part-time worker.

37
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:41,351
And then Dex came,
and he's such a good worker.

38
00:01:41,434 --> 00:01:43,144
-Hello, nice to meet you.
-Hello.

39
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,605
-Hello, it's been a while.
-Hello, Jun-ho.

40
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:49,317
TIGHT EMBRACE

41
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,485
He's Dex.

42
00:01:50,568 --> 00:01:53,196
He was in The Iron Squad,
and I loved UDT stuff as a kid.

43
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,865
DEX HAS COME TO WORK

44
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,450
Did you know about this, Boss?

45
00:01:57,534 --> 00:01:59,494
I kind of knew.

46
00:01:59,577 --> 00:02:00,411
Come on.

47
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:01,871
I didn't think he'd make it.

48
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:04,624
We were physically and mentally exhausted.

49
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:06,334
He came at the right time.

50
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:08,628
He was like rain
in the midst of a drought.

51
00:02:08,711 --> 00:02:10,964
Seeing you here, I feel so reassured.

52
00:02:11,047 --> 00:02:12,006
You can leave it to me.

53
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:13,633
DEX IS BACKING UP HIS ALLY KIAN

54
00:02:13,716 --> 00:02:16,469
I'll do my best to pull my weight here.

55
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:18,763
-He's such a good worker.
-Isn't he a good worker?

56
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:20,765
-How many days is your stay?
-It's a short stay.

57
00:02:20,849 --> 00:02:22,100
A SHORT STAY?

58
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:23,351
Just until the next night.

59
00:02:23,434 --> 00:02:24,978
-The next night?
-It's short-term.

60
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:26,146
Until tomorrow night?

61
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:28,106
But that's way too short!

62
00:02:28,189 --> 00:02:29,524
Isn't it better not to take him?

63
00:02:29,607 --> 00:02:30,441
REJECTS PART-TIMER

64
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:31,818
What are you talking about?

65
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:33,361
Isn't it better not to hire him?

66
00:02:33,444 --> 00:02:35,947
Don't be like that.
I'm a short-term part-time worker.

67
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:39,784
-But just a day is such a shame.
-I know.

68
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,411
Let's go in and show him around.

69
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,454
-Yes, show me around.
-Come on in.

70
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:44,372
Gosh, what is this?

71
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:46,332
-Is this a door?
-Yes.

72
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:47,500
DOOR

73
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:48,668
What on earth?

74
00:02:48,751 --> 00:02:50,378
I'm sure you can open this in one go.

75
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:51,462
How do you…

76
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:52,881
There you go!

77
00:02:53,548 --> 00:02:54,591
It's easy for him.

78
00:02:54,674 --> 00:02:55,633
I knew it.

79
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:57,176
HE FLIES UP AND OPENS IT IN ONE GO

80
00:02:59,137 --> 00:02:59,971
He's different.

81
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:03,933
What did you just do?

82
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:06,060
-You really open the door like this?
-Yes.

83
00:03:06,144 --> 00:03:07,812
Gosh, he got up so high.

84
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:09,647
No one's grabbed on
with both hands before.

85
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:12,066
What on earth? Do we close it like this?

86
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:14,235
I'll hold this. You pull the handle.

87
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:19,282
Pull! One.

88
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:21,117
-It's closed.
-What is this?

89
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,201
HE EASILY CLOSES IT TOO

90
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:23,953
What is this place?

91
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:27,206
It looks like a giant's…

92
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:29,626
-I feel like I've become tiny.
-It's exactly that.

93
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:30,668
That's the theme.

94
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:33,046
What is this place? It's incredible.

95
00:03:33,129 --> 00:03:34,964
-Can I go up on the sofa?
-Of course.

96
00:03:35,673 --> 00:03:36,966
LEAPS UP

97
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:38,885
AMAZED

98
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:40,428
SWINGING HIS FEET

99
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:44,724
It's like a studio apartment.
And we made it huge.

100
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:46,726
Right, it is a studio apartment.

101
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:49,687
People like staying in large rooms
when they're on trips.

102
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:51,648
So I thought, "Let's make the room big."

103
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:53,483
And I decided to make one really big room.

104
00:03:53,566 --> 00:03:55,818
How did you think of this?
It's so like you.

105
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:57,654
That's the kitchen.

106
00:03:57,737 --> 00:03:58,780
Let's go up.

107
00:03:58,863 --> 00:04:00,365
How do you get up there?

108
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:01,282
By climbing this?

109
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:03,159
Yeah, you can climb up the dishrag.

110
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,286
Because it's the kitchen?

111
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,204
EASILY

112
00:04:06,287 --> 00:04:07,455
This is incredible.

113
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:11,167
Nothing's easy here.

114
00:04:11,834 --> 00:04:13,711
Isn't this the sink, Kian?

115
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:15,296
We made it into a jacuzzi.

116
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:16,839
Gosh, this is so tough.

117
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:19,926
Kian, this place is incredible.

118
00:04:20,009 --> 00:04:22,220
The guests will use
the jacuzzi here later.

119
00:04:22,303 --> 00:04:24,514
Is this really a jacuzzi?
I thought it was the sink.

120
00:04:24,597 --> 00:04:25,473
FILLING IT WITH WATER

121
00:04:25,556 --> 00:04:27,642
-It really is a jacuzzi.
-This is so interesting.

122
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:28,685
It's original.

123
00:04:28,768 --> 00:04:30,061
-It is?
-It's so original.

124
00:04:30,144 --> 00:04:31,145
Really?

125
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:32,522
It's full of surprises.

126
00:04:32,605 --> 00:04:34,941
I thought it looked ordinary
from the outside.

127
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:37,151
But after coming inside,
I understand it now.

128
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:42,240
Kian, you have something on your face.

129
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:43,366
I'm so tired.

130
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,410
You really do look tired.

131
00:04:45,493 --> 00:04:47,245
I feel like my body's breaking down.

132
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:49,789
Really? All right.
Don't worry, Kian. Just leave it to me.

133
00:04:49,872 --> 00:04:50,707
PATTING

134
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:52,041
Thanks, man.

135
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:56,379
I can see
you're doing everything for real.

136
00:04:56,462 --> 00:04:58,715
We seriously need you right now.

137
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:00,341
You cook for them too?

138
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:02,176
-Just one meal at dinner.
-One meal?

139
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,970
What time are you leaving tomorrow?

140
00:05:04,053 --> 00:05:05,513
Make dinner before you go.

141
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:07,557
Make dinner tomorrow.

142
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:08,516
GIVING HIM WORK

143
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:11,144
I'm sure they'll be curious
about your cooking.

144
00:05:11,227 --> 00:05:12,312
Are there many ingredients?

145
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:14,230
Wait, is this a fridge?

146
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:15,148
It is.

147
00:05:18,192 --> 00:05:19,027
Geez.

148
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:21,988
Kian, I want to take this home.

149
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:24,490
Okay.

150
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:26,617
I should figure out
where everything is first.

151
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:27,827
WHILE DEX EXPLORES KITCHEN

152
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:30,038
THE SKATING GROUP

153
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:31,456
Be careful.

154
00:05:31,539 --> 00:05:32,957
-Are you okay?
-Are you okay?

155
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:36,127
THE SLEDDING GROUP

156
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:38,046
THEY'RE ALL ENJOYING THE SNOW

157
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:39,422
That was good.

158
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:40,715
You're cold, aren't you?

159
00:05:40,798 --> 00:05:42,508
-Want to go in?
-Yes.

160
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:45,511
-Let's stomp the snow off.
-Okay.

161
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:46,512
SLEDDING GROUP RETURNS

162
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:47,722
-It was fun, right?
-Yes.

163
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:49,682
-It was so fun.
-Wasn't sledding awesome?

164
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:50,767
-Should we head in?
-Yes.

165
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:51,893
SKATING GROUP RETURNS TOO

166
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:53,478
SCREECH

167
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:56,355
-Please open the door!
-Please open the door!

168
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:57,774
IS ANYONE HOME?

169
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:59,859
Maybe they can't hear us?

170
00:05:59,942 --> 00:06:02,612
Please open the door for us!

171
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:04,530
They want us to open the door.

172
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:07,200
THE PART-TIMER GOES TO HELP

173
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:08,659
You need help with the door?

174
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:10,495
-Yes.
-Thank you.

175
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:13,039
Goodness, Dex. I'm so glad you came.

176
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:15,708
It's one of the guests who came yesterday.

177
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:17,919
THE SKATING GROUP HASN'T SEEN DEX YET

178
00:06:23,674 --> 00:06:24,884
-Welcome back.
-Thank you.

179
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:27,345
-Hello. Come on in.
-Thank you.

180
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,263
STARING

181
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:30,473
Come on in.

182
00:06:33,559 --> 00:06:34,435
What?

183
00:06:34,977 --> 00:06:36,354
I'm a part-time worker.

184
00:06:36,437 --> 00:06:37,605
I'm Dex. Come on in.

185
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:40,441
I was so surprised.

186
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:42,110
I was just so surprised.

187
00:06:42,193 --> 00:06:43,361
Hello.

188
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:45,947
When did you come?

189
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:47,824
Just now.

190
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:48,991
Just now?

191
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:50,618
I had no idea.

192
00:06:50,701 --> 00:06:52,328
I thought he was just a guest.

193
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:53,746
I didn't expect it at all.

194
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:57,166
JUST AMAZED

195
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:59,001
-Did you see our part-timer?
-I did.

196
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:02,046
But you're only here for a day,
so I'm bummed.

197
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:03,798
Yeon-koung, I'll do all the work today.

198
00:07:03,881 --> 00:07:05,133
The mood's changed a bit.

199
00:07:07,051 --> 00:07:09,137
-Is it time for dinner now?
-Yes.

200
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,889
-Are these the only dishes?
-Dishes?

201
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:13,182
TONIGHT'S DINNER
KIMCHI JJIGAE

202
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:14,684
AND POTATO STIR-FRY

203
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:16,602
I'll make something.

204
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:18,020
Let me see.

205
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:20,565
THE PART-TIME WORKER WANTS
TO MAKE OTHER SIDE DISHES

206
00:07:21,357 --> 00:07:23,067
Dex, do you need help?

207
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:24,277
No, I'm good.

208
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:26,195
-You're good?
-Yes, get some rest.

209
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,155
All right.

210
00:07:27,238 --> 00:07:28,614
Can you cook?

211
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:31,451
Of course. I've been living
by myself for ten years.

212
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:33,369
I can whip something up in no time.

213
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,081
Maybe some fried eggs.

214
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:38,708
ADDITIONAL SIDE DISH
FRIED EGGS

215
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:41,711
To those who live on their own,
time is priceless.

216
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:43,713
The key is it that
needs to be easy and simple.

217
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:45,423
SIMPLEST DISH TO MAKE

218
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:49,260
You know, fried eggs and ketchup
are good enough side dishes.

219
00:07:49,343 --> 00:07:50,595
DONE IN 10 MINUTES

220
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:52,638
PUTTING A LID ON

221
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:55,057
Let's cover this up.
We can't have dust getting in.

222
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:56,225
HE KEEPS THINGS CLEAN TOO

223
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:57,852
AND NEXT

224
00:07:57,935 --> 00:07:59,562
I just need to cook the mushrooms now.

225
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:01,731
STIR-FRYING VARIOUS VEGETABLES

226
00:08:01,814 --> 00:08:03,691
Gosh, you make things in no time.

227
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:05,860
I'm just adding more options.

228
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:06,861
This should be enough.

229
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:08,863
STIR-FRY IS DONE IN 6 MINUTES

230
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:12,575
ADDITIONAL SIDE DISH 2
MUSHROOM AND VEGGIE STIR-FRY

231
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:14,702
I mixed hot pepper sauce tuna
with kimchi tuna.

232
00:08:14,785 --> 00:08:15,620
LAST SIDE DISH

233
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:17,288
-It's all done.
-All right.

234
00:08:17,371 --> 00:08:19,290
I don't like food that has cooled down.

235
00:08:19,373 --> 00:08:20,541
-So…
-You're wrapping it up?

236
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:21,626
HE WRAPS IT IN FOIL

237
00:08:21,709 --> 00:08:22,627
THOROUGHLY

238
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:25,087
It's hot since I covered it up nicely.

239
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:27,089
This is so we can serve good food.

240
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,133
DEX'S 3 ADDITIONAL SIDE DISHES

241
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:30,384
This will keep them warm.

242
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:32,845
This should be good enough.

243
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:38,601
Thanks.

244
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:40,770
KIAN'S GUARDIAN

245
00:08:40,853 --> 00:08:41,812
SLAP

246
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:46,150
It's A-rin and the others.

247
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:49,904
Why is a guest trying to open it?

248
00:08:49,987 --> 00:08:51,948
6:05 P.M.

249
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:53,741
-Hello.
-Hello.

250
00:08:53,824 --> 00:08:55,451
A-JIN, A-RIN, IN-BEOM, JUN-YEOP RETURN

251
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:56,577
-Hello.
-Hello.

252
00:08:56,661 --> 00:08:57,870
Welcome back.

253
00:08:58,579 --> 00:09:00,039
Hey, A-rin and A-jin.

254
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:03,125
-We're back.
-Hi.

255
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:04,669
You bundled up a bit more today.

256
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:05,795
-That's right.
-Yeah.

257
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:06,879
Good.

258
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:14,011
JUN-YEOP STARES AT THE KITCHEN

259
00:09:14,095 --> 00:09:16,180
THREE EMPLOYEES ON THE FLOOR

260
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:20,268
NEXT TO KIAN

261
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:22,144
THERE'S SOMEONE UNFAMILIAR

262
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:25,690
I don't believe this.

263
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:27,900
Dex is here.

264
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,694
-For real?
-It's Dex!

265
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:30,611
Seriously?

266
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:35,283
His wolf-like and sexy side profile.

267
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:37,159
I knew it was Dex.

268
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,703
-Did you see him?
-What?

269
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:39,996
Dex's there.

270
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:41,539
-What?
-What? You're lying.

271
00:09:41,622 --> 00:09:43,457
His sharp nose.

272
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:44,709
It really was Dex.

273
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:49,297
Seriously, I can't believe this.

274
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,798
They're going crazy.

275
00:09:50,881 --> 00:09:52,091
Dex.

276
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:54,468
-Yes?
-The guests who just came back…

277
00:09:54,552 --> 00:09:55,386
It's really him?

278
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:58,180
They're going crazy because of you.

279
00:09:58,264 --> 00:09:59,849
Really? Where are they?

280
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:01,976
Hello.

281
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:03,185
-Hello.
-Hello.

282
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:05,021
SEEING DEX IN REAL LIFE

283
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:10,693
Geez, you all acted so different
when you first saw me.

284
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:12,445
I feel so hurt.

285
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:13,946
My goodness.

286
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,782
-No, we've been…
-No.

287
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,035
SUDDEN AFFECTION

288
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:21,412
What was that? He suddenly did this to me.

289
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:22,538
I know.

290
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:23,706
-I'm hurt.
-All of a sudden?

291
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:25,082
It's not what you think.

292
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:26,626
We were in awe then too.

293
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:27,835
We have to…

294
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:29,754
bring the food down.

295
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:32,798
-Can you try bringing the stew down?
-The stew?

296
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:35,217
There's a basket up there.

297
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:36,135
THE BOSS'S PULLEY

298
00:10:36,218 --> 00:10:37,637
-This?
-Yeah.

299
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,013
Bring this down in here?

300
00:10:39,096 --> 00:10:40,514
LOWER THE STEW WITH THE BASKET?

301
00:10:40,598 --> 00:10:42,433
Where do I even begin? It doesn't fit.

302
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:47,563
We should find a way
to conveniently send things up and down.

303
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:52,318
-I'll sort this out, Kian.
-Okay.

304
00:10:52,401 --> 00:10:54,445
I'll make a new mode of transport.

305
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:56,947
HE BREAKS THE EXISTING PULLEY DOWN FIRST

306
00:10:57,531 --> 00:10:59,241
FINDS SOME ROPE

307
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:01,869
AND A SMALL TABLE

308
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:05,289
He's quite resourceful.

309
00:11:05,373 --> 00:11:06,791
He used to be in the UDT.

310
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:08,918
That's why.

311
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:10,753
I'll try to make something good.

312
00:11:10,836 --> 00:11:13,089
HE TIES THE ROPE TO THE TABLE LEG

313
00:11:13,172 --> 00:11:14,590
TO ANOTHER LEG

314
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:15,758
TO THE THIRD LEG

315
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:17,760
AND TO THE LAST LEG

316
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:20,096
THE UPGRADED PULLEY LOOKS GOOD

317
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:21,847
-He tied it up well.
-He's good.

318
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:23,140
Let's give it a try.

319
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:26,394
The food's coming down.

320
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:27,686
-It's coming?
-Let's go get it.

321
00:11:28,729 --> 00:11:30,356
Like this? It is pretty stable.

322
00:11:30,439 --> 00:11:32,441
STABLE

323
00:11:33,317 --> 00:11:35,528
-Like this?
-Good.

324
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:37,655
-Is it okay?
-Incredible.

325
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,657
Good. We got it.

326
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,409
JJIGAE IS DELIVERED SAFELY

327
00:11:41,992 --> 00:11:43,035
That was really stable.

328
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:44,453
Very nice.

329
00:11:45,287 --> 00:11:46,122
I'm relieved.

330
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:47,873
THE BOSS TRIES IT HIMSELF TOO

331
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:50,501
ADDITIONAL SIDE DISHES COME DOWN

332
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:54,505
Good.

333
00:11:54,588 --> 00:11:56,173
-Thank you. What's this?
-What's inside?

334
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:57,299
-It's heavy.
-What is it?

335
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:58,843
They're side dishes.

336
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:00,761
Simple ones.

337
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:02,680
They do make it look
like a generous spread.

338
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:07,601
REHEATING JUN-HO'S KIMCHI JJIGAE

339
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:09,979
-Kian, let me clean up here quickly.
-Okay.

340
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:11,605
I'll just give this a wipe down.

341
00:12:13,065 --> 00:12:15,109
It's so messy. I can't just leave it.

342
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:24,535
HE PUTS AWAY SAUCES HE USED

343
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:28,080
TIDYING UP

344
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:29,373
CONTINUOUSLY

345
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:32,168
All done.

346
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:33,127
CLEAN

347
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:34,253
It's clean now.

348
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:37,798
This is insane.

349
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:38,883
6:30 P.M.

350
00:12:40,968 --> 00:12:42,136
They're back.

351
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:43,679
-They're back.
-They're back.

352
00:12:45,014 --> 00:12:46,223
They're back.

353
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:47,516
-Welcome back.
-Sorry.

354
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,226
ICE CLIMBERS ARE BACK

355
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:50,144
EVERYONE'S BACK

356
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:52,062
Everyone, after dinner,

357
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:54,899
you can use the jacuzzi or sauna.

358
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:57,568
After that, we'll open the karaoke room.

359
00:12:58,277 --> 00:12:59,320
Let's eat.

360
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:00,988
Thank you for the food.

361
00:13:01,071 --> 00:13:03,282
Today's main chef was Jun-ho.

362
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:06,911
We used all the ingredients
we had left over

363
00:13:06,994 --> 00:13:11,790
and made kimchi jjigae,
potato and Spam stir-fry.

364
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,834
And I made some other side dishes.

365
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:15,586
-Gosh, they look good.
-There's tuna.

366
00:13:15,669 --> 00:13:17,630
There's mushroom and vegetable stir-fry.

367
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:20,716
-And fried eggs, which everyone likes.
-Fried eggs.

368
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:22,593
Please enjoy.

369
00:13:22,676 --> 00:13:23,969
-Bon appétit.
-It's self-serve.

370
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:26,639
You can take
as much as you want on your trays.

371
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:29,558
Eat up.
This is your last meal as civilians.

372
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:32,561
Why does it look like army food though?

373
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:34,188
-Thank you for the food.
-Please enjoy.

374
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:35,898
-Thank you for the food.
-Thank you.

375
00:13:39,693 --> 00:13:42,071
I didn't know how it would taste,
but it was so good.

376
00:13:42,154 --> 00:13:44,240
So I just devoured it.

377
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:45,616
DEVOURING

378
00:13:45,699 --> 00:13:46,534
This is good.

379
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:50,621
The spicy food made me feel
nice and warm inside.

380
00:13:50,704 --> 00:13:52,331
I enjoyed the kimchi jjigae the most.

381
00:13:52,414 --> 00:13:55,042
You'll be eating in the military
around this time tomorrow.

382
00:13:55,709 --> 00:13:57,044
TIME LEFT UNTIL ENLISTMENT

383
00:13:57,127 --> 00:13:58,128
-That's crazy.
-It is.

384
00:13:58,212 --> 00:13:59,713
How sad.

385
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,006
FINISHING ALL THEIR FOOD

386
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:03,425
-It's nice to see you eating so well.
-Thank you.

387
00:14:04,051 --> 00:14:06,637
By the way, are you an athlete?

388
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,806
We're PE majors.

389
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:10,015
To become PE teachers?

390
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:12,393
Because of your clothes, I thought…

391
00:14:12,476 --> 00:14:13,352
I know.

392
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:14,853
I thought you were athletes.

393
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:17,231
I often hear that I resemble
Ms. Kim Yeon-koung.

394
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:18,148
Really?

395
00:14:18,774 --> 00:14:20,943
ME?

396
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:21,860
LET ME SEE

397
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,320
I can see it.

398
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:24,446
SHE RESEMBLES YEON-KOUNG

399
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:25,823
-Really?
-Yes.

400
00:14:25,906 --> 00:14:27,449
Everyone finished all of their food.

401
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:28,742
That's so great.

402
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:29,994
CLEANUP TIME

403
00:14:30,077 --> 00:14:31,912
Push the trays this way.

404
00:14:32,663 --> 00:14:33,956
This looks delicious.

405
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:36,917
WHILE CLEANING UP FOOD WASTE

406
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,586
LEFTOVER JJIGAE

407
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:41,881
SITS DOWN PROPERLY

408
00:14:45,843 --> 00:14:47,678
-Kian.
-Am I acting like a beggar?

409
00:14:47,761 --> 00:14:50,014
What do you mean?
You've always been like this.

410
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:50,931
ALREADY USED TO IT

411
00:14:52,182 --> 00:14:53,517
-We almost ate all of it.
-Right.

412
00:14:53,601 --> 00:14:54,602
COLLECT FOOD WASTE IN POT

413
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:56,312
These are the fewest leftovers so far.

414
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:58,981
THE FEWEST LEFTOVERS IN THE PAST 7 DAYS

415
00:14:59,064 --> 00:15:00,357
The jjigae was so good.

416
00:15:00,941 --> 00:15:01,984
Come, now.

417
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:05,029
You've been working nonstop
since you arrived.

418
00:15:05,112 --> 00:15:06,989
Right. I feel bad.

419
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:08,824
-Are you okay?
-Yes, I'm totally fine.

420
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:10,618
HE GOES TO THE KITCHEN FIRST

421
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:12,620
I should go up and bring it down.

422
00:15:12,703 --> 00:15:14,830
HE LOWERS THE PULLEY QUIETLY

423
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:15,748
It's here.

424
00:15:15,831 --> 00:15:18,125
It came down quietly.
Let's move each of these up.

425
00:15:18,834 --> 00:15:21,295
RETURNING UTENSILS

426
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:23,422
-Why did you put the kitchen up here?
-What?

427
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:25,549
-That's usually where the kitchen goes.
-But…

428
00:15:28,677 --> 00:15:29,678
Nice.

429
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:31,055
Good.

430
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:33,098
It was easy since you lifted it up high.

431
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:35,017
GREAT TEAMWORK

432
00:15:40,272 --> 00:15:41,941
AFTER A SATISFYING DINNER

433
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:43,317
That was so delicious.

434
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:50,532
CHECKING WATER IN THE JACUZZI

435
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:53,535
Everyone, the jacuzzi water will get cold.

436
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:55,287
Go up if you want to use it.

437
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:57,122
Or you can use the sauna.

438
00:15:57,206 --> 00:16:00,167
At 7:30 p.m.,
they'll be open for about an hour.

439
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:01,627
JACUZZI AND SAUNA ARE BOTH OPEN

440
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:03,963
SAUNA ON THE 1ST FLOOR

441
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:05,214
Did you wash up first?

442
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:10,511
JACUZZI ON THE 2ND FLOOR

443
00:16:10,594 --> 00:16:12,054
It's so warm.

444
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:13,806
GUESTS ENTER

445
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:18,143
I feel like a fish in a bathtub.

446
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:22,022
This was Boss's ambitious creation.

447
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:24,358
-Right. It is warm.
-It's warm.

448
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:25,609
YEON-KOUNG JOINS

449
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:29,196
JACUZZI IS GETTING CROWDED

450
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:32,992
OUTSIDE THE WINDOW

451
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:34,702
It's snowing outside too.

452
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:36,495
WITH HEAVY SNOW

453
00:16:36,578 --> 00:16:38,372
We should turn on some Christmas carols.

454
00:16:38,455 --> 00:16:39,289
This is so romantic.

455
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:40,916
WHILE THEY ENJOY A ROMANTIC WINTER

456
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,584
Isn't the snow incredible?

457
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:46,463
TIME LEFT UNTIL ENLISTMENT

458
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:47,381
Hey, In-beom.

459
00:16:47,464 --> 00:16:49,508
Should we cut your hair now?

460
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:50,968
Would it be too cold outside?

461
00:16:51,051 --> 00:16:52,052
It's not that cold.

462
00:16:52,136 --> 00:16:53,595
Let's cut it all off outside.

463
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:54,680
-Let's do that.
-Okay.

464
00:16:54,763 --> 00:16:56,890
-It'll get messy here.
-Exactly.

465
00:16:56,974 --> 00:16:58,100
Let's go, Dex.

466
00:16:58,183 --> 00:17:00,310
-He's shaving his hair today?
-Yes.

467
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:01,937
He's grown it for two years.

468
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:04,064
The time has come.

469
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:06,358
DAY BEFORE ENLISTMENT
THE TIME HAS COME

470
00:17:06,442 --> 00:17:07,651
A plastic bag.

471
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:09,695
Do you have scissors?

472
00:17:09,778 --> 00:17:10,654
Yes, I have them.

473
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:14,450
KIAN'S B&B

474
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:15,868
Gosh, look at the swirling snow.

475
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:16,994
IN THE SWIRLING SNOW

476
00:17:17,077 --> 00:17:18,579
It's snowing more than earlier.

477
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:21,749
Hey, let's do it over there.

478
00:17:22,332 --> 00:17:23,751
We can cut your hair in Waterville.

479
00:17:23,834 --> 00:17:25,878
IT'S WINTERVILLE, NOT WATERVILLE

480
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:28,172
How about in here? What do you think?

481
00:17:28,255 --> 00:17:29,965
-Let's do it in the center.
-Right.

482
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,592
IN THE SKATING RINK BARBERSHOP

483
00:17:31,675 --> 00:17:32,593
You go first.

484
00:17:32,676 --> 00:17:34,762
SHAVING OUTSIDE

485
00:17:34,845 --> 00:17:36,680
I'll go first.

486
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,640
-Be careful when you take this off.
-Okay.

487
00:17:39,224 --> 00:17:40,225
A PLASTIC BAG FOR A GOWN

488
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:42,394
Hold it here so hair doesn't get in.
Sit down.

489
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:45,689
MIXED FEELINGS

490
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:46,607
Sit.

491
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:50,277
SUPER NERVOUS

492
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:52,404
It feels weird to cut someone else's hair.

493
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:53,947
Are you ready?

494
00:17:54,573 --> 00:17:55,407
Here we go.

495
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,076
-This way.
-Let's do it.

496
00:17:58,327 --> 00:17:59,745
He's grown this for two years.

497
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:01,789
HAIR HE'S GROWN FOR 2 YEARS

498
00:18:02,915 --> 00:18:04,333
SHAKING

499
00:18:06,293 --> 00:18:07,669
I'll cut it, okay?

500
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:09,046
This feels strange.

501
00:18:09,797 --> 00:18:11,173
-Here I go.
-Okay!

502
00:18:14,927 --> 00:18:16,053
It's being cut.

503
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:25,521
Hey, look.

504
00:18:26,563 --> 00:18:28,273
Hey, look at this.

505
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:30,109
Gosh, it's… Take a look at this.

506
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:31,693
This was your hair.

507
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:37,449
You're handsome, so you're still fine.

508
00:18:38,867 --> 00:18:40,119
-Does it hurt?
-No, I'm okay.

509
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:41,036
Oh, my goodness.

510
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,037
Hey, this is an honor.

511
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:44,164
Is it okay for me to touch this hair?

512
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:45,582
To cut the hair you've grown out…

513
00:18:45,666 --> 00:18:47,543
-The honor's mine.
-Thank you for this chance.

514
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:53,465
The day I left home

515
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:56,885
-Boarded the train
-Boarded the train

516
00:18:57,845 --> 00:19:03,225
-And went to boot camp
-And went to boot camp

517
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:06,895
I'll use the clippers now.

518
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:08,272
-Okay.
-What guard size is this?

519
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:09,439
It's 12 mm.

520
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:10,607
All right.

521
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:12,359
We're in the fast lane now.

522
00:19:12,442 --> 00:19:13,277
Go bold.

523
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,736
-I'll start in the middle.
-Okay.

524
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:20,075
It's being cut.

525
00:19:22,077 --> 00:19:24,830
I can't believe I'm getting
a buzz cut to become a baldy.

526
00:19:26,665 --> 00:19:28,375
-Are you distressed?
-He is.

527
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:30,335
-He must be.
-Yeah, it's indescribable.

528
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:31,253
CLOSING HIS EYES

529
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:32,629
This feeling.

530
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:34,590
We've been there too.

531
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:36,550
It feels like you're going somewhere

532
00:19:36,633 --> 00:19:38,552
-beyond the point of return.
-Right.

533
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,847
They all say it'll pass soon,

534
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:44,558
but the fact is,
time passes so slowly in there.

535
00:19:44,641 --> 00:19:45,767
It feels really long.

536
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:46,852
BRUTALLY HONEST CONSOLING

537
00:19:46,935 --> 00:19:50,647
Around this time tomorrow,
you'll have your first roll call.

538
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:53,483
-I'll have fun tonight before I go.
-You should.

539
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:55,569
But this will be
such an unforgettable memory.

540
00:19:55,652 --> 00:19:57,654
-You'll remember it forever.
-Yeah, totally.

541
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,907
You came to Kian's B&B
the day before enlistment

542
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:02,326
and got your hair shaved
out in heavy snow.

543
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:03,994
A STRANGE BARBERSHOP

544
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:06,163
I feel really strange too.

545
00:20:06,246 --> 00:20:07,372
HE BECOMES SENTIMENTAL TOO

546
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:10,584
SO SENTIMENTAL

547
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:12,461
-Are you getting choked up?
-I am.

548
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:15,547
You were going to enter together,
but you can't,

549
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:18,842
so you must feel bad.

550
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:20,260
It's almost finished.

551
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,845
-It looks cool.
-I bet you're curious.

552
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:23,555
-Yes.
-It looks cool.

553
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,515
We should hold up
a mirror for our customer.

554
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:30,729
How is it? I bet it's been ages
since you've seen your hair so short.

555
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:31,939
You don't remember, right?

556
00:20:32,022 --> 00:20:33,190
I don't.

557
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:34,650
I buzzed it very neatly.

558
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:35,984
-Nice.
-Thank you.

559
00:20:37,527 --> 00:20:39,655
IN-BEOM'S HEAD HAS BEEN SHAVED

560
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:43,367
Let me see. It looks good.

561
00:20:44,117 --> 00:20:45,285
He looks even more handsome.

562
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:46,620
This is better.

563
00:20:46,703 --> 00:20:48,038
-This is better?
-It is.

564
00:20:48,121 --> 00:20:49,665
-Because you're handsome.
-Yeah.

565
00:20:49,748 --> 00:20:51,541
I'll make a safe return from the military.

566
00:20:51,625 --> 00:20:52,709
TIME LEFT UNTIL ENLISTMENT

567
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:53,627
Salute!

568
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:55,128
VERY SATISFIED BARBER

569
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,213
He's a soldier already.

570
00:20:56,296 --> 00:20:58,340
-Please cut my hair too.
-Yes, let's cut yours too.

571
00:20:58,423 --> 00:20:59,466
Our second customer.

572
00:20:59,549 --> 00:21:01,260
We will begin the shaving ceremony.

573
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:02,386
Right away.

574
00:21:04,137 --> 00:21:05,013
What on earth?

575
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:07,140
A BIG WAD OF HAIR

576
00:21:07,224 --> 00:21:10,018
Maybe since it's your second time,
you're not hesitating at all.

577
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:11,103
WITHOUT HESITATION

578
00:21:11,186 --> 00:21:13,480
Maybe like this? Let me see.

579
00:21:17,901 --> 00:21:19,736
Come on, hurry up and cut it nicely.

580
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:21,530
You have to do this first though.

581
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:22,948
Right, a shave down the middle.

582
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:24,616
First, a shave down the middle.

583
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:28,620
Gosh, what is this feeling?

584
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:31,623
This feels so strange.

585
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:34,293
-All done.
-It was cut nicely.

586
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:35,585
-Okay.
-Well done.

587
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:36,795
JUN-YEOP HAS BEEN SHAVED TOO

588
00:21:37,462 --> 00:21:39,506
I'll make sure to come back
safe and sound too.

589
00:21:40,215 --> 00:21:41,758
I hope you two take care as you serve.

590
00:21:41,842 --> 00:21:43,135
But how do you feel?

591
00:21:43,218 --> 00:21:45,554
Your friend did this together for you.

592
00:21:47,347 --> 00:21:48,473
You…

593
00:21:49,182 --> 00:21:50,183
Why did you do it?

594
00:21:51,893 --> 00:21:52,811
Hey.

595
00:21:52,894 --> 00:21:55,147
If you think about it,
he was being a loyal friend.

596
00:21:55,230 --> 00:21:56,982
LOYAL BUZZ CUT DUO

597
00:21:57,065 --> 00:21:58,233
So we shaved…

598
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:02,404
We shaved our heads.

599
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:05,073
I couldn't let my friend do it alone.

600
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:06,616
For the remaining month,

601
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:08,618
I was going to think of it
as being in the army,

602
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:10,537
so I cut my hair with him.

603
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:14,875
I'm touched that he'd go that far for me.

604
00:22:14,958 --> 00:22:17,336
They wished me good luck in the military.

605
00:22:17,419 --> 00:22:20,464
It was very heartwarming.

606
00:22:20,547 --> 00:22:21,465
Okay.

607
00:22:22,549 --> 00:22:23,884
You look good though.

608
00:22:23,967 --> 00:22:25,260
You look good too.

609
00:22:26,094 --> 00:22:26,928
My hair.

610
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:28,096
HAIR AS A MEMENTO

611
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,514
Keep it with you.

612
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:30,891
The back of their heads!

613
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:32,934
That's a familiar sight.

614
00:22:33,602 --> 00:22:36,480
Hey, now that they've cut their hair,
it feels so real.

615
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:44,237
I think I've always seen life
from my own perspective.

616
00:22:44,321 --> 00:22:45,530
"This is how soldiers feel."

617
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:47,991
But this time, it went beyond that.

618
00:22:48,075 --> 00:22:50,452
They're young enough to be my nephews.

619
00:22:50,535 --> 00:22:52,370
I cut their hair as an elder,

620
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:54,539
so it felt a bit strange.

621
00:22:56,374 --> 00:22:58,293
This was actually made
to be a skating rink.

622
00:22:58,376 --> 00:22:59,419
-This spot?
-Yeah.

623
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:01,088
-Gosh.
-Now, it feels like a barbershop.

624
00:23:01,171 --> 00:23:02,339
BARBERSHOP IS CLOSED

625
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:07,302
They must've cut their hair.

626
00:23:08,386 --> 00:23:09,387
They shaved their heads.

627
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:12,182
-Did they shave their heads?
-They did.

628
00:23:12,265 --> 00:23:13,642
It looks good on you.

629
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:16,061
Hey, it looks good on you.

630
00:23:16,144 --> 00:23:17,229
Okay.

631
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:18,355
You look cool.

632
00:23:18,438 --> 00:23:19,648
-You look handsome.
-Thank you.

633
00:23:20,649 --> 00:23:21,942
They both cut their hair.

634
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:24,820
-Mr. Kian, I'll take the clippers.
-Okay.

635
00:23:24,903 --> 00:23:26,279
-I'll clean them.
-Okay.

636
00:23:27,447 --> 00:23:30,283
THEY CHECK THEIR APPEARANCES

637
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:33,286
Does it feel different
because I cut it for you?

638
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:34,621
-Of course.
-Really?

639
00:23:34,704 --> 00:23:36,081
-It means a lot to us.
-Right.

640
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:38,250
It's not bad?

641
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:40,210
IT'S NOT BAD

642
00:23:40,293 --> 00:23:41,169
They said it's okay.

643
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:42,087
FEELING PROUD

644
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:43,630
A SELFIE TO COMMEMORATE

645
00:23:43,713 --> 00:23:44,548
MEANWHILE

646
00:23:44,631 --> 00:23:46,091
What was your major again?

647
00:23:46,174 --> 00:23:47,342
I'm a nursing major.

648
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:49,719
Are you preparing to look for jobs now?

649
00:23:49,803 --> 00:23:52,055
No, I'm running a small YouTube channel.

650
00:23:52,139 --> 00:23:53,682
LEE SU-RYEON
NURSING MAJOR, YOUTUBER

651
00:23:53,765 --> 00:23:55,392
I'm a college student too.

652
00:23:55,475 --> 00:23:56,309
What?

653
00:23:56,393 --> 00:23:58,353
I'm a PE major
at Korea National Open University.

654
00:23:58,436 --> 00:23:59,813
I enrolled in 2024.

655
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:01,565
We enrolled in 2024 too.

656
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:02,649
HEY, FELLOW STUDENT

657
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:05,068
-You're attending college right now?
-Yes.

658
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:06,528
Do you have the time?

659
00:24:06,611 --> 00:24:08,613
I take classes online.

660
00:24:09,489 --> 00:24:11,032
-So you're going to be juniors?
-Yes.

661
00:24:11,116 --> 00:24:12,993
I'm going to be a junior too.

662
00:24:13,076 --> 00:24:15,162
But my grades were bad last semester,

663
00:24:15,245 --> 00:24:17,414
so I'm not sure
if I'll be able to graduate, but…

664
00:24:17,497 --> 00:24:18,832
WORRIED ABOUT HER GRADES

665
00:24:19,708 --> 00:24:21,209
You're living life to the fullest.

666
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:22,878
Goodness.

667
00:24:23,420 --> 00:24:24,796
Everyone seems happy.

668
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:26,715
They become close
and get sad when they leave.

669
00:24:26,798 --> 00:24:28,717
Really? Has anyone ever cried?

670
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:29,926
I almost cried.

671
00:24:30,010 --> 00:24:32,262
-You did?
-You know, on their last days…

672
00:24:32,345 --> 00:24:34,556
-You become attached very quickly here.
-Right.

673
00:24:34,639 --> 00:24:37,434
This room makes that possible
because it brings people together.

674
00:24:37,517 --> 00:24:38,810
I think so too.

675
00:24:38,894 --> 00:24:42,731
Guests want to interact with us.

676
00:24:42,814 --> 00:24:45,775
-Right.
-And the others are so good with that.

677
00:24:45,859 --> 00:24:48,695
Yeon-koung's especially good.
Maybe it's because she's older.

678
00:24:48,778 --> 00:24:50,530
Yeah, she's very easy to approach.

679
00:24:51,156 --> 00:24:52,616
My little sister.

680
00:24:52,699 --> 00:24:53,533
My older sister.

681
00:24:53,617 --> 00:24:55,327
I guess I should accept
that we look alike.

682
00:24:55,410 --> 00:24:56,369
My little sister.

683
00:24:56,995 --> 00:24:59,122
Zuha's good too.

684
00:24:59,206 --> 00:25:00,373
She does a good job.

685
00:25:00,999 --> 00:25:01,833
Jun-ho too.

686
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:03,001
TALKING ABOUT ANIMALS

687
00:25:04,753 --> 00:25:06,588
I'm the worst one at interacting.

688
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:09,466
-But you have your own way.
-Right.

689
00:25:10,634 --> 00:25:12,677
I can't bother to get changed,
so I'll just go in.

690
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:16,056
Welcome. Isn't this the best?

691
00:25:16,139 --> 00:25:17,057
JOINS TO INTERACT

692
00:25:17,140 --> 00:25:18,350
I love it.

693
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:20,185
I should sweat it out a bit here.

694
00:25:21,478 --> 00:25:22,646
This is so nice.

695
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:26,274
I should get some rest.

696
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:27,901
PART-TIME WORKER TAKES A REST

697
00:25:27,984 --> 00:25:29,277
Let's go to the sauna.

698
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:30,779
This is so fun.

699
00:25:31,404 --> 00:25:32,948
You can take your time.

700
00:25:33,031 --> 00:25:34,282
EXODUS FROM THE JACUZZI

701
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:35,200
Hello.

702
00:25:35,909 --> 00:25:37,202
I'm back.

703
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:38,119
A FULL SAUNA

704
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,246
Everyone ends up here.

705
00:25:41,081 --> 00:25:42,457
MAKING IT HOTTER

706
00:25:47,712 --> 00:25:49,631
IT'S GETTING HOTTER

707
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:50,548
See the sweat?

708
00:25:50,632 --> 00:25:52,050
-I feel it.
-Me too.

709
00:25:52,759 --> 00:25:54,511
-Want to go run with our shirts off?
-What?

710
00:25:55,095 --> 00:25:56,930
-Want to go? Let's go.
-Yes.

711
00:25:57,013 --> 00:25:58,306
THEY SUDDENLY GO OUT?

712
00:25:58,390 --> 00:25:59,766
Let's face the cold.

713
00:26:02,185 --> 00:26:03,270
In our bare feet?

714
00:26:03,353 --> 00:26:04,354
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

715
00:26:05,313 --> 00:26:06,481
Let's go!

716
00:26:07,190 --> 00:26:08,441
SU-RYEON JOINS TOO

717
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:12,445
LATE-NIGHT SNOWBALL FIGHT

718
00:26:12,529 --> 00:26:13,446
Take off your shirts.

719
00:26:18,535 --> 00:26:20,328
COOLING DOWN SAUNA HEAT WITH SNOW

720
00:26:22,539 --> 00:26:23,915
It's so cold!

721
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,667
It was something I did dream of doing.

722
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:27,627
I loved that the most.

723
00:26:27,711 --> 00:26:28,795
It's so cold!

724
00:26:28,878 --> 00:26:30,171
THE BOSS IS CAPTURED

725
00:26:30,255 --> 00:26:31,339
It's so cold!

726
00:26:37,470 --> 00:26:38,305
It's so cold.

727
00:26:38,388 --> 00:26:39,723
RUNNING AWAY

728
00:26:39,806 --> 00:26:40,849
Should we go too?

729
00:26:40,932 --> 00:26:42,851
ZUHA AND CHOI SISTERS JOIN TOO

730
00:26:44,311 --> 00:26:45,145
It's cold!

731
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:51,568
It was so fun. It was so romantic.

732
00:26:54,112 --> 00:26:54,946
It's cold!

733
00:26:55,697 --> 00:26:57,115
It's so cold!

734
00:26:58,241 --> 00:26:59,075
Gosh, it's cold.

735
00:27:04,539 --> 00:27:05,665
STRAIGHT BACK INTO THE SAUNA

736
00:27:05,749 --> 00:27:06,583
Amazing.

737
00:27:07,167 --> 00:27:08,001
Incredible.

738
00:27:08,793 --> 00:27:11,880
THEY ENJOY GOING
BETWEEN HOT AND COLD AREAS

739
00:27:11,963 --> 00:27:13,256
This is pretty fun.

740
00:27:13,923 --> 00:27:15,467
It's fun, isn't it?

741
00:27:16,301 --> 00:27:18,345
He threw snow at my mouth.

742
00:27:18,428 --> 00:27:20,805
-I made a snowball right away.
-It went down your throat?

743
00:27:21,431 --> 00:27:22,432
Really?

744
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:25,060
THE BOSS GETS OUT

745
00:27:25,143 --> 00:27:25,977
I'm so hot.

746
00:27:29,939 --> 00:27:32,692
HE PUTS BACK ON CLOTHES HE TOOK OFF

747
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:38,073
AND RESTS IN THAT STATE

748
00:27:38,156 --> 00:27:39,324
Isn't this so nice?

749
00:27:39,407 --> 00:27:40,367
EVEN AFTER THAT

750
00:27:40,450 --> 00:27:41,368
"Control yourself."

751
00:27:42,285 --> 00:27:43,953
"I'm going to tell my boyfriend."

752
00:27:45,413 --> 00:27:47,957
THEY BECOME CLOSER IN THE SAUNA

753
00:27:48,041 --> 00:27:49,417
It's Squid Game.

754
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:51,169
-In Squid Game?
-Yes.

755
00:27:51,753 --> 00:27:52,837
8:30 P.M.

756
00:27:52,921 --> 00:27:54,130
Should I have some beer?

757
00:27:55,590 --> 00:27:57,425
Hey, those…

758
00:27:57,509 --> 00:27:58,343
Hold on.

759
00:27:58,426 --> 00:27:59,386
They must be frozen.

760
00:27:59,469 --> 00:28:00,303
-What?
-What?

761
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:01,888
-It's been a while.
-The ones outside?

762
00:28:01,971 --> 00:28:02,806
Yeah, the beer.

763
00:28:02,889 --> 00:28:04,140
-There's beer outside?
-Yeah.

764
00:28:05,892 --> 00:28:07,018
Push me.

765
00:28:08,603 --> 00:28:09,604
Let's go.

766
00:28:11,898 --> 00:28:12,732
Where are they?

767
00:28:14,025 --> 00:28:15,110
Gosh, look at this.

768
00:28:15,193 --> 00:28:16,444
Is this it? These are beers?

769
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:17,529
The snow's piled up.

770
00:28:18,279 --> 00:28:20,198
BEER WAS KEPT IN SNOW

771
00:28:20,281 --> 00:28:22,325
-My feet are so cold.
-It's so cold.

772
00:28:24,619 --> 00:28:26,079
Let's have some cold beer.

773
00:28:26,162 --> 00:28:27,330
LATE NIGHT SNACK TIME

774
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:28,832
-Come over here.
-Okay.

775
00:28:28,915 --> 00:28:30,667
-Hey, over here.
-Come sit with us.

776
00:28:30,750 --> 00:28:31,626
Bring some soda.

777
00:28:31,709 --> 00:28:32,752
THE KIDS BRING SODA

778
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:35,964
THEY TALK IN SMALL GROUPS

779
00:28:36,047 --> 00:28:38,466
How do you feel? It's your last night.

780
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:39,384
I don't want to go.

781
00:28:39,467 --> 00:28:40,760
THE FOUR CHECK OUT TOMORROW

782
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:42,429
Did you talk much with the staff?

783
00:28:42,512 --> 00:28:45,223
-With Zuha.
-We talked a lot with her.

784
00:28:45,306 --> 00:28:46,975
-We were basically stuck on her.
-Really?

785
00:28:47,058 --> 00:28:48,101
Yes, we talked a lot.

786
00:28:48,184 --> 00:28:51,521
I did see you
interact with female guests a lot.

787
00:28:51,604 --> 00:28:53,314
-Right. It was fun.
-She was the best.

788
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:55,900
We'll never get to have
this kind of experience again.

789
00:28:55,984 --> 00:28:57,360
-I've been so happy.
-Right.

790
00:28:57,444 --> 00:28:58,945
That's so good to hear.

791
00:28:59,028 --> 00:28:59,863
RELIEVED

792
00:28:59,946 --> 00:29:00,864
Right.

793
00:29:02,198 --> 00:29:03,533
HE TAKES OFF HIS WATCH

794
00:29:03,616 --> 00:29:04,909
-You bought one, right?
-Yes.

795
00:29:04,993 --> 00:29:06,077
You're entering in April?

796
00:29:06,161 --> 00:29:07,454
A SOLDIER'S MUST-HAVE ITEM

797
00:29:07,537 --> 00:29:08,371
Oh, my.

798
00:29:09,038 --> 00:29:10,999
-A watch-giving ceremony.
-It's nothing fancy.

799
00:29:11,624 --> 00:29:12,459
Still.

800
00:29:13,251 --> 00:29:15,336
WATCH-AWARDING CEREMONY

801
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:16,546
That's awesome.

802
00:29:16,629 --> 00:29:18,423
Hey. We're pretty cool, aren't we?

803
00:29:18,506 --> 00:29:20,091
We cut your hair and gave you a watch.

804
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:22,135
I quite liked that watch too.

805
00:29:22,761 --> 00:29:24,554
I'm sure the battery
will last a long time.

806
00:29:24,637 --> 00:29:27,140
So it'll last until you finish
your military service.

807
00:29:27,223 --> 00:29:28,767
-Thank you.
-Don't lose it.

808
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:30,310
-I'll never lose it.
-Good.

809
00:29:30,393 --> 00:29:32,979
Anyway, it felt strange
when I was cutting your hair.

810
00:29:33,062 --> 00:29:33,897
Really?

811
00:29:34,439 --> 00:29:36,149
It felt so strange. It was just…

812
00:29:37,901 --> 00:29:39,611
It felt weird for some reason.

813
00:29:39,694 --> 00:29:43,156
It reminded me a little bit
of my younger self

814
00:29:43,239 --> 00:29:46,534
and made me think
about how much time has passed.

815
00:29:46,618 --> 00:29:49,329
And I know it'll be tough
for you in many ways.

816
00:29:53,708 --> 00:29:56,127
I have no watch now.
Hey, I'll give it to you when you leave.

817
00:29:56,211 --> 00:29:57,086
I still need it.

818
00:29:57,170 --> 00:29:58,379
-Tell me when you leave.
-Okay.

819
00:29:58,463 --> 00:29:59,798
-I'm not taking it back.
-Right.

820
00:29:59,881 --> 00:30:00,715
TAKING IT BACK

821
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:01,883
He took it back.

822
00:30:01,966 --> 00:30:02,926
He had it taken away.

823
00:30:03,009 --> 00:30:04,511
I still really need it.

824
00:30:05,762 --> 00:30:07,639
CHECKING TIME FOR KARAOKE

825
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:10,892
TIME LEFT UNTIL ENLISTMENT

826
00:30:10,975 --> 00:30:13,561
When I go in tomorrow,
I'm sure I'll miss this place a lot.

827
00:30:14,437 --> 00:30:16,231
What are you going to do once he leaves?

828
00:30:16,314 --> 00:30:17,315
You'll be so lonely.

829
00:30:17,398 --> 00:30:20,401
We go way back. We've gone to
all the same schools together.

830
00:30:20,485 --> 00:30:23,112
He's my good friend. My dearest friend.

831
00:30:23,196 --> 00:30:24,781
STARING

832
00:30:24,864 --> 00:30:26,574
I think he really likes him a lot.

833
00:30:26,658 --> 00:30:28,117
-Jun-yeop likes In-beom?
-One-sided?

834
00:30:28,201 --> 00:30:29,452
-He likes him more.
-Really?

835
00:30:29,536 --> 00:30:31,871
And he doesn't show it.

836
00:30:32,413 --> 00:30:34,123
But he likes his friend too on the inside.

837
00:30:34,207 --> 00:30:35,667
That's why they're friends.

838
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:39,504
And Mr. Kian said
he also had a friend like him.

839
00:30:39,587 --> 00:30:43,758
EMOTIONALLY INVESTED

840
00:30:44,884 --> 00:30:47,470
Let me give you
the watch again before I forget.

841
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:50,265
I'll just look at my phone
to check the time.

842
00:30:51,099 --> 00:30:53,351
HE PUTS IT ON HIM AGAIN

843
00:30:53,434 --> 00:30:56,479
What are you high schoolers
interested in these days?

844
00:30:56,563 --> 00:30:58,231
-Everyone's into K-pop idols.
-Right.

845
00:30:58,314 --> 00:31:01,568
I heard Yun-woo's phone wallpaper
was a photo of Kazuha.

846
00:31:01,651 --> 00:31:03,069
-That's right.
-Really?

847
00:31:03,152 --> 00:31:05,989
And Seong-bhin's was a photo of me.

848
00:31:07,156 --> 00:31:08,491
Would you like to see it?

849
00:31:08,575 --> 00:31:09,409
Really?

850
00:31:09,492 --> 00:31:11,244
Seong-bhin, please. Don't.

851
00:31:11,327 --> 00:31:12,328
GOSH, PUT IT AWAY

852
00:31:12,412 --> 00:31:13,746
Give it to me.

853
00:31:13,830 --> 00:31:14,664
What?

854
00:31:15,915 --> 00:31:17,917
Seong-bhin, I told you not to do this.

855
00:31:18,001 --> 00:31:18,835
Jun-ho.

856
00:31:22,714 --> 00:31:24,048
I can't believe you.

857
00:31:24,132 --> 00:31:26,509
-Is that Yeon-koung?
-Yeah, it's me.

858
00:31:26,593 --> 00:31:28,344
-When I don't want to study…
-You use it?

859
00:31:28,428 --> 00:31:29,762
A GOOD STIMULUS FOR STUDYING

860
00:31:30,346 --> 00:31:34,726
Once, I read Cosmos,
and my brain became all jumbled.

861
00:31:34,809 --> 00:31:37,312
-But space really was interesting.
-Right.

862
00:31:37,937 --> 00:31:40,106
I mean, we as humans
struggle so hard to survive.

863
00:31:40,189 --> 00:31:41,024
Right.

864
00:31:41,107 --> 00:31:45,945
Then, when I became aware of
the universe or stars, it suddenly felt…

865
00:31:46,029 --> 00:31:46,863
Right.

866
00:31:46,946 --> 00:31:50,074
-Everything felt so insignificant.
-Insignificant.

867
00:31:50,158 --> 00:31:50,992
THEY STRONGLY AGREE

868
00:31:51,075 --> 00:31:51,910
The vast universe.

869
00:31:51,993 --> 00:31:54,412
Sometimes, it makes me feel at peace.

870
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:58,333
What I thought about recently
was this one sentence in the book

871
00:31:58,416 --> 00:32:01,169
about larger clusters existing
beyond our solar system.

872
00:32:01,252 --> 00:32:03,504
After I saw that,
I talked about it with my mom.

873
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:06,090
By the way,
what do your parents do for work?

874
00:32:06,883 --> 00:32:09,260
They're not in the science field.

875
00:32:09,344 --> 00:32:12,221
I just talk with them about space.

876
00:32:12,305 --> 00:32:16,726
Still, they need to have
some knowledge about it to talk with you.

877
00:32:16,809 --> 00:32:19,062
I think they like science programs.

878
00:32:19,145 --> 00:32:22,941
Really? Did they grow
to like them because of you?

879
00:32:23,024 --> 00:32:25,068
Or have they always liked those shows?

880
00:32:25,151 --> 00:32:29,113
They became interested because of me
and started watching them more.

881
00:32:29,197 --> 00:32:32,283
They see and ask me about things
from those shows that I don't know.

882
00:32:32,367 --> 00:32:35,078
My case is similar.
When I was active in Japan,

883
00:32:35,161 --> 00:32:38,748
my parents wanted to share interests
with me, so they studied Japanese.

884
00:32:38,831 --> 00:32:40,083
Really?

885
00:32:40,166 --> 00:32:41,960
So, that helped us communicate.

886
00:32:42,043 --> 00:32:44,712
And sometimes, I'd even talk
in Japanese with my mom.

887
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:48,216
If your parents hadn't always done that,

888
00:32:48,299 --> 00:32:51,094
it means they studied it just for you.

889
00:32:51,177 --> 00:32:52,595
-I'm grateful.
-You should be.

890
00:32:53,179 --> 00:32:55,014
-They're such good parents.
-You think so?

891
00:32:55,098 --> 00:32:57,225
KIAN'S B&B

892
00:32:57,809 --> 00:32:58,643
Boss.

893
00:32:58,726 --> 00:33:00,228
Didn't you say you'd be the host?

894
00:33:01,062 --> 00:33:01,896
Are we starting?

895
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:03,815
Okay. Then, shall we get ready?

896
00:33:03,898 --> 00:33:04,732
All right.

897
00:33:05,441 --> 00:33:07,360
-Mr. Kian!
-Let's go!

898
00:33:07,443 --> 00:33:09,904
HE GOES TO DRESS UP FOR KARAOKE

899
00:33:10,571 --> 00:33:12,281
FINISHED CHANGING

900
00:33:12,365 --> 00:33:13,366
What?

901
00:33:13,449 --> 00:33:15,243
He's dressed up. Oh, my gosh.

902
00:33:15,326 --> 00:33:16,911
HIS SUIT CATCHES THEIR ATTENTION

903
00:33:16,995 --> 00:33:18,079
The host.

904
00:33:18,162 --> 00:33:20,123
-This is going to be so fun.
-Our host, Kian.

905
00:33:21,290 --> 00:33:23,084
9:00 P.M.
KARAOKE ROOM IS OPEN

906
00:33:23,167 --> 00:33:24,836
-Okay.
-How are you, everyone?

907
00:33:27,588 --> 00:33:30,049
We have just two days left now
at Kian's B&B.

908
00:33:30,133 --> 00:33:31,509
KIAN'S B&B CLOSES IN 2 DAYS

909
00:33:31,592 --> 00:33:33,177
-Two days left.
-I'm so sad.

910
00:33:33,261 --> 00:33:36,639
Anyway, I'd been thinking all day
about how to make things fun for you

911
00:33:36,723 --> 00:33:38,182
during your stay.

912
00:33:38,266 --> 00:33:41,644
It's hard. It always is,
but I'm doing my best.

913
00:33:41,728 --> 00:33:43,271
So…

914
00:33:43,354 --> 00:33:45,398
I hope you enjoy your stay!

915
00:33:45,481 --> 00:33:47,525
-Okay!
-Okay!

916
00:33:47,608 --> 00:33:49,902
We're going to perform a duet.

917
00:33:51,070 --> 00:33:52,530
WITH WHO?

918
00:33:53,364 --> 00:33:55,241
ME!

919
00:33:58,703 --> 00:34:02,206
SETTING THE STAGE

920
00:34:02,874 --> 00:34:04,751
Shall we get started? Right away?

921
00:34:05,585 --> 00:34:06,836
NERVOUS

922
00:34:06,919 --> 00:34:07,837
Here we go.

923
00:34:09,547 --> 00:34:15,219
WHAT WILL BE THE FIRST PERFORMANCE?

924
00:34:16,971 --> 00:34:17,805
Oh, my.

925
00:34:19,932 --> 00:34:21,768
JUST HEARING THE INTRO MAKES HIM TEAR UP

926
00:34:21,851 --> 00:34:23,603
-Oh, no.
-Gosh, he's going to cry.

927
00:34:23,686 --> 00:34:25,813
It seems they're singing it for you guys.

928
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:28,399
"A LETTER FROM A PRIVATE"
BY KIM KWANG-SEOK

929
00:34:28,483 --> 00:34:30,985
-They're going in.
-This is dedicated to our two young men.

930
00:34:31,486 --> 00:34:34,030
The day I left home

931
00:34:34,947 --> 00:34:37,450
Boarded the train

932
00:34:39,494 --> 00:34:44,582
And went to boot camp

933
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:51,839
After I bowed deeply to my parents

934
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:53,925
TIME LEFT UNTIL ENLISTMENT

935
00:34:54,008 --> 00:34:59,097
And walked out the front gate

936
00:34:59,931 --> 00:35:01,516
Take care, In-beom.

937
00:35:02,141 --> 00:35:03,351
-Stay safe.
-Take care.

938
00:35:03,434 --> 00:35:05,686
-Take care of yourself.
-Good luck in April.

939
00:35:07,855 --> 00:35:10,817
My hair…

940
00:35:10,900 --> 00:35:13,236
-After it was cut short
-After it was cut short

941
00:35:15,071 --> 00:35:20,535
-Looked funny at first
-Looked funny at first

942
00:35:22,245 --> 00:35:25,331
-But my smile
-But my smile

943
00:35:25,414 --> 00:35:29,502
-In the mirror
-In the mirror

944
00:35:29,585 --> 00:35:35,299
-Falls along with my heart
-Falls along with my heart

945
00:35:36,843 --> 00:35:43,516
-If I go up on the nearby hill
-If I go up on the nearby hill

946
00:35:44,225 --> 00:35:47,687
-Will I be able to see my town?
-Will I be able to see my town?

947
00:35:47,770 --> 00:35:48,771
GETTING CHOKED UP

948
00:35:51,274 --> 00:35:57,446
Now, it's time to start again

949
00:35:58,906 --> 00:36:04,704
The dreams of my youth

950
00:36:10,293 --> 00:36:12,128
I'm getting choked up.

951
00:36:13,254 --> 00:36:15,715
Since it's our last night tonight,

952
00:36:16,465 --> 00:36:17,466
we picked this song.

953
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:21,095
IN-BEOM AND JUN-YEOP'S RESPONSE
TO FIRST SONG

954
00:36:21,971 --> 00:36:23,764
"After This Night"!

955
00:36:25,016 --> 00:36:27,476
"AFTER THIS NIGHT"
BY YIM JAE-BEUM

956
00:36:34,233 --> 00:36:35,776
KIAN'S B&B KARAOKE

957
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:41,616
On this night full of lights

958
00:36:42,450 --> 00:36:46,287
A sad farewell is approaching

959
00:36:47,246 --> 00:36:52,585
But I still have a lot of things
I want to say

960
00:36:57,340 --> 00:37:02,803
After this night passes

961
00:37:02,887 --> 00:37:07,141
We'll have to part ways once again

962
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:10,603
-What on earth? He's good.
-Yeah, In-beom's a good singer.

963
00:37:10,686 --> 00:37:15,691
Without even saying a word like this

964
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:17,068
Like this!

965
00:37:17,151 --> 00:37:20,363
Do I have to let you go?

966
00:37:20,446 --> 00:37:21,864
EXPLOSION OF EMOTIONS

967
00:37:24,742 --> 00:37:26,619
-He's so different when singing.
-Incredible!

968
00:37:26,702 --> 00:37:28,454
Good luck in the military!

969
00:37:28,537 --> 00:37:30,957
Salute! Good luck!

970
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:34,252
That was an awesome performance.

971
00:37:34,335 --> 00:37:35,670
Did you prepare anything?

972
00:37:35,753 --> 00:37:37,672
She can do some cheerleading.

973
00:37:37,755 --> 00:37:39,382
I want to see her be a cheerleader.

974
00:37:39,465 --> 00:37:40,591
-Cheerleading.
-Cheerleading.

975
00:37:40,675 --> 00:37:43,803
SHE GOES TO SHOW HER CHEERLEADING

976
00:37:45,137 --> 00:37:46,138
She didn't hesitate.

977
00:37:46,222 --> 00:37:48,349
"HIGHWAY IN THE GALE"
BY YU JUNG-SEOK

978
00:37:48,432 --> 00:37:51,602
Give me one more gale of courage

979
00:37:51,686 --> 00:37:54,188
CHEERING WITH KARAOKE WIGS

980
00:37:54,272 --> 00:37:58,359
So I won't succumb to the rough waves

981
00:37:58,442 --> 00:38:00,528
Look at how she's moving her body.

982
00:38:00,611 --> 00:38:06,367
Hope to leave a new mark on the vast land

983
00:38:06,450 --> 00:38:11,330
I'll hold onto it and run to you

984
00:38:19,630 --> 00:38:20,464
All together now!

985
00:38:20,548 --> 00:38:24,844
Give me one more gale of courage

986
00:38:24,927 --> 00:38:26,512
UP AND DOWN

987
00:38:26,595 --> 00:38:28,723
So I won't succumb…

988
00:38:28,806 --> 00:38:30,182
A WAVE WITH ARMS AROUND SHOULDERS

989
00:38:30,266 --> 00:38:33,185
ENTHUSIASTIC

990
00:38:33,269 --> 00:38:36,439
Hope to leave a new mark on the vast land

991
00:38:36,522 --> 00:38:39,066
IN A TRANCE

992
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:43,571
I'll hold onto it and run to you

993
00:38:44,822 --> 00:38:46,699
To you

994
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:49,285
Thank you.

995
00:38:49,952 --> 00:38:50,995
Nice!

996
00:38:51,704 --> 00:38:53,080
That was great!

997
00:38:54,040 --> 00:38:56,417
-Let's go, A-rin and A-jin.
-Here they finally come.

998
00:38:56,500 --> 00:38:57,335
Finally.

999
00:38:57,418 --> 00:38:58,836
A-rin and A-jin.

1000
00:38:58,919 --> 00:39:00,379
I wonder what they'll sing.

1001
00:39:01,714 --> 00:39:02,715
What on earth?

1002
00:39:02,798 --> 00:39:05,801
You're so cute! You look so cute!

1003
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:07,178
-What?
-What is this?

1004
00:39:07,261 --> 00:39:09,263
This song?

1005
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:14,226
DANCING FURIOUSLY

1006
00:39:17,063 --> 00:39:18,397
SHOCKED

1007
00:39:18,481 --> 00:39:20,775
They're suddenly so hyper.

1008
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:24,362
A DAZZLING PERFORMANCE

1009
00:39:24,445 --> 00:39:26,489
Very nice!

1010
00:39:26,572 --> 00:39:28,115
Get up!

1011
00:39:28,199 --> 00:39:29,867
-Get up.
-Get up!

1012
00:39:34,163 --> 00:39:36,248
Everyone's out of their mind

1013
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:37,166
Everyone!

1014
00:39:37,249 --> 00:39:40,669
They're all going crazy

1015
00:39:40,753 --> 00:39:44,173
Who can I trust? How can I?
I can't trust them anymore

1016
00:39:44,256 --> 00:39:47,301
Yeah, that's right!
Don't trust anyone!

1017
00:39:47,385 --> 00:39:51,972
You and everyone else
in this world are shallow

1018
00:39:54,016 --> 00:39:56,644
Change, change, change it!

1019
00:39:56,727 --> 00:39:58,479
Change everything!

1020
00:39:58,562 --> 00:40:01,982
Change, change, change all of it!

1021
00:40:02,066 --> 00:40:05,444
Change, change, change the lies!

1022
00:40:05,528 --> 00:40:08,823
Change, change, change the whole world!

1023
00:40:10,366 --> 00:40:12,410
A-rin and A-jin, you crushed it!

1024
00:40:12,493 --> 00:40:13,327
You crushed it!

1025
00:40:13,411 --> 00:40:15,496
-This is what I'm talking about!
-This is awesome!

1026
00:40:15,579 --> 00:40:17,123
A DOPAMINE RUSH

1027
00:40:17,206 --> 00:40:18,624
Make some noise!

1028
00:40:18,707 --> 00:40:20,292
IT'S NOT OVER YET

1029
00:40:20,376 --> 00:40:22,044
JUMPING UP AND DOWN

1030
00:40:26,090 --> 00:40:27,341
You're amazing!

1031
00:40:28,717 --> 00:40:30,803
-He's so cute.
-He looks like a squirrel.

1032
00:40:33,180 --> 00:40:34,432
THE KARAOKE ROOM

1033
00:40:34,515 --> 00:40:36,892
IS IN A FRENZY

1034
00:40:37,476 --> 00:40:39,520
THE BOSS IS IN A FRENZY

1035
00:40:40,146 --> 00:40:42,273
KIAN'S B&B IS HEATING UP

1036
00:40:45,776 --> 00:40:46,819
They're so excited.

1037
00:40:46,902 --> 00:40:48,988
They pretty much all know how to have fun.

1038
00:40:49,071 --> 00:40:50,364
Especially today.

1039
00:40:51,115 --> 00:40:53,284
-They're mostly singing upbeat songs.
-Right.

1040
00:40:55,327 --> 00:40:56,912
Well, Boss? Are you satisfied?

1041
00:40:56,996 --> 00:40:58,664
-I'm so happy.
-Right?

1042
00:40:58,747 --> 00:40:59,790
I'm so happy.

1043
00:40:59,874 --> 00:41:01,208
He says he's so happy.

1044
00:41:01,292 --> 00:41:04,003
Happy? He's happy today?

1045
00:41:04,086 --> 00:41:05,671
-That's a relief.
-It is.

1046
00:41:05,754 --> 00:41:08,215
HAPPY

1047
00:41:08,299 --> 00:41:11,010
KIAN'S B&B KARAOKE

1048
00:41:11,093 --> 00:41:12,344
Are you going to bed now?

1049
00:41:12,428 --> 00:41:13,721
Yeah, I am.

1050
00:41:13,804 --> 00:41:15,014
Let's brush our teeth.

1051
00:41:15,097 --> 00:41:16,932
THE HIGH SCHOOLERS GO TO BED FIRST

1052
00:41:17,016 --> 00:41:21,103
Listen. They're still high schoolers,

1053
00:41:21,187 --> 00:41:22,730
so they have to go to bed.

1054
00:41:22,813 --> 00:41:24,523
I think we should
let them sleep in a room.

1055
00:41:24,607 --> 00:41:25,441
-Sure.
-Of course.

1056
00:41:25,524 --> 00:41:26,609
MORE THAN HAPPY TO

1057
00:41:27,193 --> 00:41:28,611
THANKS TO THE GIRLS

1058
00:41:28,694 --> 00:41:30,321
-This is nice and cozy.
-I know.

1059
00:41:30,404 --> 00:41:33,073
THEY CAN SLEEP COMFORTABLY

1060
00:41:33,157 --> 00:41:34,241
10:00 P.M.

1061
00:41:34,325 --> 00:41:35,409
I have a question.

1062
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:38,996
You made some insane comments
on Single's Inferno.

1063
00:41:39,079 --> 00:41:40,039
Like in a good way.

1064
00:41:40,122 --> 00:41:44,627
Did you really come up
with those comments on your own?

1065
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:48,339
I just said those things
when I was feeling extremely shy,

1066
00:41:48,422 --> 00:41:49,673
but people liked that.

1067
00:41:51,550 --> 00:41:52,801
So, I was pretty surprised.

1068
00:41:52,885 --> 00:41:55,554
The time when you grabbed the flag,
that was so…

1069
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:57,848
I really liked the swimming pool scene.

1070
00:41:57,932 --> 00:41:59,183
Shall I do it for you?

1071
00:42:01,143 --> 00:42:02,895
HATES IT

1072
00:42:04,688 --> 00:42:05,856
Hold on!

1073
00:42:07,274 --> 00:42:08,901
FAINTING

1074
00:42:10,653 --> 00:42:12,321
She was so overwhelmed that she fainted.

1075
00:42:12,404 --> 00:42:13,864
I was so happy.

1076
00:42:14,907 --> 00:42:16,283
She's loving it.

1077
00:42:19,078 --> 00:42:20,704
I'm grateful you came.

1078
00:42:20,788 --> 00:42:21,914
MEANWHILE

1079
00:42:21,997 --> 00:42:24,708
And for letting me cut
the hair you'd grown for two years,

1080
00:42:25,459 --> 00:42:26,502
thank you so much.

1081
00:42:26,585 --> 00:42:28,587
-You look cool with a buzz cut.
-I'm so grateful.

1082
00:42:28,671 --> 00:42:30,297
What time do you enter boot camp?

1083
00:42:30,381 --> 00:42:32,299
-At 2:00 p.m.
-At 2:00 p.m.?

1084
00:42:32,383 --> 00:42:33,717
The countdown begins.

1085
00:42:33,801 --> 00:42:35,469
TIME LEFT UNTIL ENLISTMENT

1086
00:42:35,553 --> 00:42:38,597
I don't know
if we'll cross paths in the future,

1087
00:42:38,681 --> 00:42:41,225
but I hope we do in someplace cool.

1088
00:42:43,143 --> 00:42:44,478
Let's all do our best.

1089
00:42:45,980 --> 00:42:46,981
Cheers.

1090
00:42:52,945 --> 00:42:54,196
We should go to bed.

1091
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:56,699
Everyone, you can just
leave things there and go to bed.

1092
00:42:56,782 --> 00:42:58,367
Go to bed. We'll clean it up tomorrow.

1093
00:42:58,450 --> 00:43:00,077
Hey, Jun-yeop and In-beom.

1094
00:43:00,160 --> 00:43:00,995
Yes?

1095
00:43:01,078 --> 00:43:03,664
I heard you're leaving early
in the morning. This is my book.

1096
00:43:03,747 --> 00:43:05,624
YEON-KOUNG SAYS GOODBYE WITH GIFTS

1097
00:43:05,708 --> 00:43:06,792
-Thank you.
-Give it a read.

1098
00:43:06,875 --> 00:43:07,710
I will.

1099
00:43:07,793 --> 00:43:08,919
-Good luck.
-In the military…

1100
00:43:09,003 --> 00:43:10,212
Okay, I'll root for you.

1101
00:43:10,296 --> 00:43:11,422
Take care.

1102
00:43:11,505 --> 00:43:12,673
-Thank you.
-All right.

1103
00:43:12,756 --> 00:43:14,341
-Bye. It was nice meeting you.
-Goodbye.

1104
00:43:14,425 --> 00:43:15,551
I'll root for you too.

1105
00:43:15,634 --> 00:43:17,219
-Bye.
-Bye. Good luck.

1106
00:43:18,679 --> 00:43:20,514
-Good night.
-Good night.

1107
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:22,391
-See you in the morning.
-See you.

1108
00:43:23,851 --> 00:43:24,977
What about Young-geon?

1109
00:43:25,060 --> 00:43:26,770
-There.
-Up there? Okay.

1110
00:43:26,854 --> 00:43:27,855
-Good night.
-Good night.

1111
00:43:27,938 --> 00:43:28,772
FRIDGE

1112
00:43:29,356 --> 00:43:30,190
HANGERS

1113
00:43:30,274 --> 00:43:31,567
Good work today, everyone.

1114
00:43:32,151 --> 00:43:34,862
LIVING ROOM

1115
00:43:34,945 --> 00:43:36,322
-Good night.
-Good night.

1116
00:43:36,405 --> 00:43:37,990
TV CABINET

1117
00:43:38,073 --> 00:43:42,661
EVERYONE IS SOUND ASLEEP

1118
00:43:42,745 --> 00:43:46,040
5:00 A.M.

1119
00:43:47,499 --> 00:43:50,127
IN-BEOM AND JUN-YEOP WRITE LETTERS

1120
00:43:51,003 --> 00:43:51,837
Let's go.

1121
00:43:53,714 --> 00:43:56,467
Let's move our suitcases to the door
and wake Mr. Kian up.

1122
00:43:56,550 --> 00:43:57,760
Okay.

1123
00:44:00,763 --> 00:44:02,181
Mr. Kian.

1124
00:44:02,973 --> 00:44:04,642
We're checking out now.

1125
00:44:05,559 --> 00:44:07,645
-You're leaving now?
-Yes, we're going now.

1126
00:44:15,736 --> 00:44:17,279
We wrote letters.

1127
00:44:17,863 --> 00:44:19,782
-To the others too?
-Yes.

1128
00:44:19,865 --> 00:44:20,991
Bye. Take care.

1129
00:44:21,075 --> 00:44:22,493
-Thank you. Bye.
-Goodbye.

1130
00:44:23,077 --> 00:44:24,787
-Bye.
-Please go back to sleep.

1131
00:44:24,870 --> 00:44:25,704
Good night.

1132
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:31,043
KNOCKS OUT

1133
00:44:43,222 --> 00:44:45,891
THE SNOW IS KNEE-DEEP

1134
00:44:49,311 --> 00:44:50,145
What on earth?

1135
00:44:51,397 --> 00:44:52,648
It's cold.

1136
00:44:52,731 --> 00:44:54,650
It hasn't been that cold, but it is today.

1137
00:44:55,359 --> 00:44:56,777
Three days passed by so fast.

1138
00:44:58,278 --> 00:45:00,406
It was our last trip
before entering the military,

1139
00:45:00,489 --> 00:45:04,201
so I went in happy and thought,
"Let's have a blast one last time."

1140
00:45:05,494 --> 00:45:08,247
I got to share this unique experience
with Jun-yeop.

1141
00:45:08,831 --> 00:45:11,542
It felt like I'd gone back
to how we played as kids.

1142
00:45:11,625 --> 00:45:13,085
I was able to be more honest

1143
00:45:13,669 --> 00:45:15,462
and bolder.

1144
00:45:15,546 --> 00:45:17,423
It was a perfect and special time.

1145
00:45:18,006 --> 00:45:21,927
Even when I'm old,
I think I'll keep replaying this moment.

1146
00:45:23,011 --> 00:45:25,180
We should take one last look
before we leave.

1147
00:45:28,767 --> 00:45:29,810
Bye, Kian's B&B.

1148
00:45:29,893 --> 00:45:33,147
5:30 A.M.
IN-BEOM AND JUN-YEOP CHECK OUT

1149
00:45:33,772 --> 00:45:36,233
EVEN AFTER THEY CHECK OUT

1150
00:45:36,817 --> 00:45:38,694
IT KEEPS SNOWING

1151
00:45:38,777 --> 00:45:41,447
KIAN'S B&B

1152
00:45:42,698 --> 00:45:44,992
IT'S BEEN SNOWING HEAVILY FOR 30 HOURS

1153
00:45:45,075 --> 00:45:47,161
IN DAEGWALLYEONG

1154
00:45:47,244 --> 00:45:49,246
SNOW BUILDUP HAS REACHED 40 CM

1155
00:45:50,038 --> 00:45:53,000
DUE TO OVERNIGHT SNOWFALL,
ROADS ARE EXPECTED TO BE ICY

1156
00:45:54,501 --> 00:45:56,670
DAY 8

1157
00:45:56,753 --> 00:45:58,547
KIAN'S B&B CLOSES IN 1 DAY

1158
00:45:58,630 --> 00:46:00,841
KIAN'S B&B

1159
00:46:02,718 --> 00:46:05,721
7:30 A.M.

1160
00:46:30,704 --> 00:46:31,955
It's so cold.

1161
00:46:37,461 --> 00:46:40,631
DEX TRIES PUTTING A SOCK ON

1162
00:46:44,468 --> 00:46:46,345
GIVES UP

1163
00:46:48,764 --> 00:46:50,807
BLINKING

1164
00:46:51,600 --> 00:46:54,394
HE GETS UP IN THE END

1165
00:46:55,604 --> 00:46:56,730
Good morning.

1166
00:46:56,813 --> 00:46:58,148
-Hello.
-Hello.

1167
00:47:04,112 --> 00:47:05,572
GUESTS WAKE UP ONE BY ONE

1168
00:47:05,656 --> 00:47:07,115
What time is it?

1169
00:47:07,199 --> 00:47:08,116
It's 8:00 a.m.

1170
00:47:11,411 --> 00:47:14,081
THE BOSS WAKES UP TOO

1171
00:47:15,374 --> 00:47:16,750
-Did you sleep well?
-Yes.

1172
00:47:17,584 --> 00:47:19,044
-Hyeon-seo.
-Yes?

1173
00:47:19,127 --> 00:47:20,128
Did you sleep well?

1174
00:47:20,212 --> 00:47:21,547
Yes, I did.

1175
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:23,173
It was so cozy. I liked it.

1176
00:47:23,257 --> 00:47:25,050
-He's adorable.
-I know.

1177
00:47:27,970 --> 00:47:29,263
THEY TRY TO TURN ON THE LIGHTS

1178
00:47:29,346 --> 00:47:30,847
-Hold on.
-Try it this way.

1179
00:47:32,266 --> 00:47:34,393
-This won't work.
-I told you that won't work.

1180
00:47:37,229 --> 00:47:38,564
Are you playing volleyball?

1181
00:47:38,647 --> 00:47:39,773
-Go on.
-Please do it for us.

1182
00:47:39,856 --> 00:47:40,691
-Me?
-Yes.

1183
00:47:40,774 --> 00:47:42,359
I'm not that good at this.

1184
00:47:47,197 --> 00:47:48,574
It's really difficult.

1185
00:47:48,657 --> 00:47:49,491
WATCHING

1186
00:47:55,789 --> 00:47:56,832
ONE SHOT

1187
00:47:56,915 --> 00:47:59,084
ONE KILL

1188
00:48:00,794 --> 00:48:02,170
-Olé!
-She did it.

1189
00:48:02,254 --> 00:48:03,880
Olé, olé!

1190
00:48:03,964 --> 00:48:05,716
-Olé!
-Oh, my gosh.

1191
00:48:05,799 --> 00:48:07,009
Olé.

1192
00:48:07,968 --> 00:48:09,636
Aren't you leaving today?

1193
00:48:09,720 --> 00:48:11,096
We are.

1194
00:48:11,179 --> 00:48:12,431
A-JIN AND A-RIN CHECK OUT TODAY

1195
00:48:12,514 --> 00:48:15,559
Hey, it's my birthday today.
Can't you leave later?

1196
00:48:15,642 --> 00:48:16,893
-Seriously?
-Yes.

1197
00:48:16,977 --> 00:48:18,270
-Today?
-Today's your birthday?

1198
00:48:18,353 --> 00:48:20,439
-Happy birthday to you
-Happy birthday to you

1199
00:48:20,522 --> 00:48:21,356
SHY

1200
00:48:21,440 --> 00:48:22,691
Is it someone's birthday?

1201
00:48:22,774 --> 00:48:24,026
Whose is it?

1202
00:48:24,109 --> 00:48:25,611
-Whose?
-Whose birthday is it?

1203
00:48:25,694 --> 00:48:26,945
-Hyeon-seo's.
-Hyeon-seo's?

1204
00:48:27,029 --> 00:48:28,864
-Today?
-Yes, it's today.

1205
00:48:28,947 --> 00:48:30,449
-Happy birthday.
-Really?

1206
00:48:30,532 --> 00:48:31,992
We should get a cake later.

1207
00:48:32,075 --> 00:48:33,118
Right.

1208
00:48:33,201 --> 00:48:34,411
Let's go, Seo-young.

1209
00:48:34,494 --> 00:48:35,329
Okay, sure.

1210
00:48:35,412 --> 00:48:37,414
We'll get going.

1211
00:48:37,497 --> 00:48:39,207
THE GUESTS GO ON A TRIP

1212
00:48:39,291 --> 00:48:40,584
-Bye.
-Have a nice trip.

1213
00:48:40,667 --> 00:48:41,710
See you later.

1214
00:48:41,793 --> 00:48:43,295
Have a nice trip!

1215
00:48:43,378 --> 00:48:44,755
Happy birthday, Hyeon-seo.

1216
00:48:44,838 --> 00:48:45,964
Thank you.

1217
00:48:46,048 --> 00:48:47,549
When you come back later, we'll give…

1218
00:48:47,633 --> 00:48:48,592
birthday punches.

1219
00:48:51,303 --> 00:48:53,180
I've never seen this much snow before.

1220
00:48:53,263 --> 00:48:54,348
GUESTS GO OUT

1221
00:48:54,431 --> 00:48:56,850
A-JIN AND A-RIN GET READY TO CHECK OUT

1222
00:48:56,933 --> 00:48:59,186
Right, the guys wrote letters
for us before leaving.

1223
00:48:59,269 --> 00:49:01,021
They wrote letters?

1224
00:49:06,109 --> 00:49:07,653
He wrote them with his left hand.

1225
00:49:07,736 --> 00:49:09,696
BECAUSE JUN-YEOP HURT HIS RIGHT HAND

1226
00:49:09,780 --> 00:49:11,531
They're so nice.

1227
00:49:11,615 --> 00:49:12,741
They have kind hearts.

1228
00:49:12,824 --> 00:49:14,368
Are you feeling okay?

1229
00:49:14,451 --> 00:49:16,119
I feel so worn out, you know?

1230
00:49:16,203 --> 00:49:17,621
I can't even work out properly.

1231
00:49:18,246 --> 00:49:19,956
Anyway, I'm sad we have to leave soon.

1232
00:49:20,040 --> 00:49:21,291
I want to stay a bit longer.

1233
00:49:21,375 --> 00:49:23,669
YEON-KOUNG IS SAD THAT IT WILL END

1234
00:49:23,752 --> 00:49:24,920
Stay a few more days then.

1235
00:49:25,003 --> 00:49:26,713
We'll shoot for a few more days.

1236
00:49:26,797 --> 00:49:27,714
Want to do it?

1237
00:49:28,423 --> 00:49:30,258
-Thanks for the gesture.
-Yeah?

1238
00:49:30,342 --> 00:49:32,052
Even if you don't mean it, thanks.

1239
00:49:32,135 --> 00:49:35,222
No, I really feel sad
that we have to part ways.

1240
00:49:35,305 --> 00:49:37,891
Why are you suddenly crying?

1241
00:49:37,974 --> 00:49:41,103
He's… Kian's crying. Oh, no.

1242
00:49:42,062 --> 00:49:44,231
-Don't cry.
-What? Okay.

1243
00:49:50,445 --> 00:49:51,738
We have to leave now.

1244
00:49:54,199 --> 00:49:55,367
You're leaving?

1245
00:49:55,450 --> 00:49:56,618
You're going? I see.

1246
00:49:56,702 --> 00:49:58,412
Thank you so much. Where did it go?

1247
00:49:58,495 --> 00:50:00,205
-You wrote letters?
-Yes.

1248
00:50:00,288 --> 00:50:01,456
-Really?
-Oh, my gosh.

1249
00:50:03,041 --> 00:50:04,376
THEY WROTE THEM LAST NIGHT

1250
00:50:04,459 --> 00:50:07,713
WE MADE FOND MEMORIES
AND WE WERE HAPPY FOR 3 DAYS

1251
00:50:07,796 --> 00:50:09,589
FROM THE CHOI SISTERS

1252
00:50:09,673 --> 00:50:11,383
Thank you.

1253
00:50:11,466 --> 00:50:13,135
Oh, my.

1254
00:50:13,218 --> 00:50:15,429
Your karaoke performance last night
was so cool.

1255
00:50:15,512 --> 00:50:17,013
You were the best.

1256
00:50:17,097 --> 00:50:18,724
Did you enjoy your stay?

1257
00:50:18,807 --> 00:50:20,809
-Yes, we had so much fun.
-Really?

1258
00:50:20,892 --> 00:50:23,687
Thanks to you, we had so much fun too.

1259
00:50:23,770 --> 00:50:25,147
SAD

1260
00:50:25,230 --> 00:50:27,190
But a three-day stay's too short.

1261
00:50:27,274 --> 00:50:28,316
-I know.
-Seriously.

1262
00:50:28,400 --> 00:50:30,277
We just got close, and you have to leave.

1263
00:50:30,360 --> 00:50:32,154
-Have a safe trip.
-Have a safe trip.

1264
00:50:32,738 --> 00:50:33,572
Be happy.

1265
00:50:33,655 --> 00:50:34,656
Okay.

1266
00:50:34,740 --> 00:50:36,366
-Be happy too.
-Thank you.

1267
00:50:36,450 --> 00:50:37,784
Goodbye.

1268
00:50:37,868 --> 00:50:39,369
-Good luck!
-Good luck!

1269
00:50:40,328 --> 00:50:42,998
KIAN'S B&B

1270
00:50:43,915 --> 00:50:45,667
-Let's go.
-I don't want to go.

1271
00:50:45,751 --> 00:50:49,171
We'd been so busy with life
before we came here.

1272
00:50:49,254 --> 00:50:52,424
Then, we let ourselves go
and had fun at Kian's B&B.

1273
00:50:52,507 --> 00:50:54,801
It felt like going to karaoke after exams.

1274
00:50:54,885 --> 00:50:58,638
I think this trip was
the happiest moment in my life.

1275
00:50:58,722 --> 00:50:59,848
Bye, Kian's B&B.

1276
00:50:59,931 --> 00:51:02,017
Bye, Kian's B&B. For real.

1277
00:51:02,100 --> 00:51:04,603
A-JIN AND A-RIN CHECK OUT

1278
00:51:07,189 --> 00:51:09,733
What now? Should we clean up?

1279
00:51:10,484 --> 00:51:11,818
I'm too tired to clean up.

1280
00:51:11,902 --> 00:51:13,570
How about we don't do it?

1281
00:51:13,653 --> 00:51:14,571
Let's not do it.

1282
00:51:16,198 --> 00:51:18,325
There won't be
any new guests today, right?

1283
00:51:18,408 --> 00:51:20,368
-There won't be.
-There better not be.

1284
00:51:20,452 --> 00:51:22,329
We had too many guests yesterday.

1285
00:51:22,913 --> 00:51:23,747
Then,

1286
00:51:24,915 --> 00:51:26,875
let's clean and…

1287
00:51:26,958 --> 00:51:28,543
Leave the kitchen to me.

1288
00:51:28,627 --> 00:51:30,337
I like your energy.

1289
00:51:30,420 --> 00:51:32,047
Let's hang in there.

1290
00:51:32,130 --> 00:51:33,590
-Okay, let's go!
-Let's go!

1291
00:51:33,673 --> 00:51:34,758
Let's keep going!

1292
00:51:34,841 --> 00:51:36,593
-Okay!
-It's our last night!

1293
00:51:39,137 --> 00:51:42,140
I mean, we clean every day,
but it's always a mess.

1294
00:51:44,976 --> 00:51:46,436
Gosh, why is everything…

1295
00:51:48,104 --> 00:51:49,314
Boss.

1296
00:51:49,397 --> 00:51:51,900
How can you brush your teeth
when we're all cleaning?

1297
00:51:51,983 --> 00:51:53,360
Let me just brush my teeth first.

1298
00:51:53,443 --> 00:51:55,529
You should be cleaning the floor,
not your teeth.

1299
00:51:56,112 --> 00:51:57,405
I'm sorry.

1300
00:51:57,489 --> 00:51:59,699
My teeth are also part
of the cleaning area.

1301
00:52:01,576 --> 00:52:02,994
They're in the cleaning area here.

1302
00:52:03,078 --> 00:52:04,120
Is that so?

1303
00:52:04,204 --> 00:52:05,872
CLEANING HARD

1304
00:52:05,956 --> 00:52:07,582
THE BOSS IS CLEANING HIS OWN AREA

1305
00:52:08,291 --> 00:52:11,086
I haven't washed trays
since I was discharged from the military.

1306
00:52:20,554 --> 00:52:21,805
How did you hang these?

1307
00:52:28,520 --> 00:52:29,980
But…

1308
00:52:30,063 --> 00:52:31,481
why are you hanging them?

1309
00:52:31,565 --> 00:52:33,108
We don't have any new guests.

1310
00:52:33,191 --> 00:52:35,318
I guess he wanted to do it too.

1311
00:52:37,487 --> 00:52:38,822
How did you do this?

1312
00:52:39,823 --> 00:52:42,409
HE MANAGES TO HANG ONE

1313
00:52:43,034 --> 00:52:44,244
I can't do it anymore.

1314
00:52:44,828 --> 00:52:46,246
HE GIVES UP FAST

1315
00:52:46,329 --> 00:52:47,747
I wanted to give it a try.

1316
00:52:49,749 --> 00:52:51,209
All done!

1317
00:52:51,793 --> 00:52:52,836
Good work.

1318
00:52:53,628 --> 00:52:56,715
Now that we have one more person,
we finished by 11:00 a.m.

1319
00:52:56,798 --> 00:52:59,009
-I know.
-What time did you usually finish before?

1320
00:52:59,092 --> 00:53:00,218
After 1:00 p.m.

1321
00:53:00,302 --> 00:53:01,219
-Really?
-Yeah.

1322
00:53:01,303 --> 00:53:02,846
We finished so fast today.

1323
00:53:02,929 --> 00:53:04,306
-What should we eat?
-Let's see.

1324
00:53:04,389 --> 00:53:06,224
What does our part-time worker want?

1325
00:53:06,308 --> 00:53:07,976
"Korean beef from Daegwallyeong."

1326
00:53:08,059 --> 00:53:08,894
Korean beef?

1327
00:53:08,977 --> 00:53:09,978
INTERESTED

1328
00:53:10,061 --> 00:53:10,979
Do you want meat?

1329
00:53:11,062 --> 00:53:13,189
I know it's lunch,
but I'm craving barbecue.

1330
00:53:13,273 --> 00:53:14,190
Okay, let's go here.

1331
00:53:14,274 --> 00:53:15,150
KOREAN BEEF FOR LUNCH

1332
00:53:15,233 --> 00:53:16,610
Let's go!

1333
00:53:16,693 --> 00:53:17,944
Let's go.

1334
00:53:18,028 --> 00:53:20,155
It just won't stop snowing.

1335
00:53:20,238 --> 00:53:21,364
It's so deep.

1336
00:53:21,448 --> 00:53:23,074
UP TO ZUHA'S KNEES

1337
00:53:23,158 --> 00:53:24,409
It's unbelievable.

1338
00:53:24,492 --> 00:53:26,661
I've never seen so much snow.

1339
00:53:26,745 --> 00:53:28,121
Is it like 20 or 30 cm of snow?

1340
00:53:28,204 --> 00:53:29,164
ABOUT 50 CM

1341
00:53:29,247 --> 00:53:30,582
The scenery's amazing.

1342
00:53:35,295 --> 00:53:36,379
This is just incredible.

1343
00:53:37,005 --> 00:53:38,465
-This is crazy.
-Look at the scenery.

1344
00:53:38,548 --> 00:53:39,758
Cows are just out there.

1345
00:53:39,841 --> 00:53:41,426
Is it not cold for them?

1346
00:53:41,509 --> 00:53:43,178
Wait, I forgot something.

1347
00:53:43,261 --> 00:53:44,471
YEON-KOUNG GOES BACK TO GET IT

1348
00:53:45,639 --> 00:53:46,681
WASHING HIS FACE WITH SNOW

1349
00:53:46,765 --> 00:53:48,099
-You're washing your face?
-Yeah.

1350
00:53:48,600 --> 00:53:49,768
For goodness' sake.

1351
00:53:50,560 --> 00:53:52,479
THEN HE TASTES THE SNOW

1352
00:53:52,562 --> 00:53:53,813
It's just like sherbet.

1353
00:53:53,897 --> 00:53:55,106
-Did you eat it?
-Try it.

1354
00:53:56,191 --> 00:53:57,859
-You ate it?
-Have you eaten snow before?

1355
00:53:57,943 --> 00:54:00,445
-I haven't.
-He's having a bite right now.

1356
00:54:03,073 --> 00:54:04,908
-Is this right?
-Have a bite?

1357
00:54:04,991 --> 00:54:06,201
JUN-HO HAS A BITE TOO

1358
00:54:06,284 --> 00:54:07,911
-Here.
-Thank you.

1359
00:54:07,994 --> 00:54:09,412
Have a bite.

1360
00:54:09,496 --> 00:54:10,789
ZUHA HAS A BITE TOO

1361
00:54:10,872 --> 00:54:12,123
Is it good?

1362
00:54:12,207 --> 00:54:13,166
It's like shaved ice.

1363
00:54:13,249 --> 00:54:14,709
DEX TRIES IT TOO

1364
00:54:14,793 --> 00:54:15,710
It's good.

1365
00:54:16,336 --> 00:54:17,587
It seems delicious to me.

1366
00:54:17,671 --> 00:54:19,547
-It's shaved ice.
-We could make bingsu.

1367
00:54:19,631 --> 00:54:22,342
Right? It'll be like sherbet
if we add flavorings.

1368
00:54:22,425 --> 00:54:24,010
-We just need condensed milk.
-Yeah.

1369
00:54:24,094 --> 00:54:25,762
-Yeon-koung.
-Yeah?

1370
00:54:25,845 --> 00:54:27,263
Taste some of the snow.

1371
00:54:28,932 --> 00:54:29,849
Eat it?

1372
00:54:30,433 --> 00:54:31,434
Why are you eating snow?

1373
00:54:31,518 --> 00:54:32,560
Because it's clean.

1374
00:54:32,644 --> 00:54:33,603
I'm good.

1375
00:54:34,688 --> 00:54:35,772
Why would you eat snow?

1376
00:54:36,481 --> 00:54:38,400
I can't believe I just ate snow.

1377
00:54:38,483 --> 00:54:41,987
-Wait, three have to sit in the back.
-Yeah.

1378
00:54:42,070 --> 00:54:43,822
Is there enough space?

1379
00:54:44,572 --> 00:54:45,740
Dex, you sit in the front.

1380
00:54:45,824 --> 00:54:47,283
-Yes.
-Is that okay?

1381
00:54:47,367 --> 00:54:49,411
-I'll sit in the middle.
-Thank you.

1382
00:54:49,494 --> 00:54:51,871
Since I'm a part-time worker,
Kian's being so thoughtful.

1383
00:54:51,955 --> 00:54:52,789
It's so cramped.

1384
00:54:52,872 --> 00:54:54,666
-This is so uncomfortable.
-It's so cramped!

1385
00:54:54,749 --> 00:54:56,292
It's so cramped.

1386
00:54:56,876 --> 00:55:00,088
Could you not push me with your shoulder?

1387
00:55:00,171 --> 00:55:01,047
SHOULDER PRESSED DOWN

1388
00:55:01,131 --> 00:55:02,465
No, I moved it forward for you.

1389
00:55:02,549 --> 00:55:04,092
Your shoulders are quite broad.

1390
00:55:04,175 --> 00:55:05,760
Because I was an athlete.

1391
00:55:05,844 --> 00:55:07,512
Or I'll move back
and you push me down.

1392
00:55:07,595 --> 00:55:09,055
-Like this?
-Yeah.

1393
00:55:09,139 --> 00:55:10,348
It's uncomfortable.

1394
00:55:10,432 --> 00:55:11,474
Rest yours on mine.

1395
00:55:11,558 --> 00:55:12,642
Rest it?

1396
00:55:13,226 --> 00:55:14,769
It's so uncomfortable back here.

1397
00:55:16,062 --> 00:55:18,690
Jun-ho, I think it's better
to be driving today.

1398
00:55:20,650 --> 00:55:22,652
-Sorry, but…
-Sorry, but can you go faster?

1399
00:55:24,571 --> 00:55:26,865
Jun-ho, we've traveled comfortably
thanks to you.

1400
00:55:26,948 --> 00:55:28,992
-Right.
-Don't mention it.

1401
00:55:29,075 --> 00:55:30,827
How has it been lately, Boss?

1402
00:55:30,910 --> 00:55:33,079
As time has gone on,
it's gotten better.

1403
00:55:33,163 --> 00:55:34,789
-Really?
-Really? Better?

1404
00:55:34,873 --> 00:55:36,791
Ever since Smita said that…

1405
00:55:37,417 --> 00:55:39,711
You were all bright like light,

1406
00:55:39,794 --> 00:55:42,005
but it's off now.

1407
00:55:42,088 --> 00:55:43,298
The light's off?

1408
00:55:43,381 --> 00:55:44,841
My light is off now?

1409
00:55:44,924 --> 00:55:46,718
-You can feel that?
-Yes.

1410
00:55:47,427 --> 00:55:49,971
-Right, you've changed.
-You came to your senses.

1411
00:55:50,055 --> 00:55:51,139
THE BOSS WOKE UP AFTER THAT

1412
00:55:51,222 --> 00:55:54,601
I also thought
you'd changed a lot since then.

1413
00:55:54,684 --> 00:55:56,102
And Kazuha's tears.

1414
00:55:56,186 --> 00:55:58,897
What? Zuha's tears?

1415
00:55:58,980 --> 00:56:00,648
I asked, "Are you having a tough time?"

1416
00:56:00,732 --> 00:56:02,776
And then he said, "Zuha, I'm sorry."

1417
00:56:02,859 --> 00:56:04,027
Toot!

1418
00:56:04,110 --> 00:56:06,196
Wait. I farted then?

1419
00:56:06,279 --> 00:56:07,113
NIGHT 3

1420
00:56:07,197 --> 00:56:09,074
We're grateful that you joined us.
I mean it.

1421
00:56:09,157 --> 00:56:09,991
TOOT

1422
00:56:10,075 --> 00:56:11,534
-Sorry.
-Did you fart?

1423
00:56:11,618 --> 00:56:12,994
-You farted then.
-You farted then!

1424
00:56:13,078 --> 00:56:13,953
Seriously?

1425
00:56:14,037 --> 00:56:15,455
That's so lame.

1426
00:56:15,955 --> 00:56:17,040
Geez, that's so lame.

1427
00:56:17,123 --> 00:56:18,917
Did you check your underwear then?

1428
00:56:19,000 --> 00:56:19,834
To see If he pooped?

1429
00:56:19,918 --> 00:56:23,797
He'd been wearing the same pair
of underpants for three days already.

1430
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:25,381
I checked.

1431
00:56:25,465 --> 00:56:28,176
No wonder why he changed
his underwear after that.

1432
00:56:28,259 --> 00:56:30,136
-That's crazy.
-After three days.

1433
00:56:30,220 --> 00:56:31,304
Thank you for driving us.

1434
00:56:31,387 --> 00:56:33,306
-We're here.
-Thank you.

1435
00:56:33,389 --> 00:56:34,724
-This is nice.
-This is nice.

1436
00:56:35,433 --> 00:56:36,976
It's over after we clean up tomorrow.

1437
00:56:37,060 --> 00:56:37,894
CLOSING TOMORROW

1438
00:56:37,977 --> 00:56:40,146
I can't believe tomorrow's the last day.

1439
00:56:40,230 --> 00:56:42,148
I think I'll miss it.

1440
00:56:42,232 --> 00:56:43,608
I've worked you so hard.

1441
00:56:44,192 --> 00:56:45,777
-Hello.
-Hello.

1442
00:56:45,860 --> 00:56:47,028
-Hello.
-It's here.

1443
00:56:47,112 --> 00:56:48,988
I can't believe we're having Korean beef.

1444
00:56:49,072 --> 00:56:50,198
Put it on.

1445
00:56:50,281 --> 00:56:52,117
-Should we start grilling?
-Sure.

1446
00:56:52,200 --> 00:56:53,409
It looks so good.

1447
00:56:54,244 --> 00:56:55,453
It won't take long to cook.

1448
00:56:55,537 --> 00:56:56,704
-Right.
-Yes.

1449
00:56:56,788 --> 00:56:57,956
You can eat it now.

1450
00:56:58,039 --> 00:56:59,666
Thank you for the food.

1451
00:56:59,749 --> 00:57:00,875
Bon appétit.

1452
00:57:03,503 --> 00:57:04,796
Hey, this meat is so good.

1453
00:57:04,879 --> 00:57:06,214
-To die for?
-It's insane.

1454
00:57:13,221 --> 00:57:14,347
This is so good.

1455
00:57:15,807 --> 00:57:17,642
Hey, eat up.

1456
00:57:17,725 --> 00:57:19,060
Oh, my.

1457
00:57:22,772 --> 00:57:24,232
KIAN FINALLY TRIES SOME

1458
00:57:24,315 --> 00:57:25,733
It's so nice to eat out.

1459
00:57:25,817 --> 00:57:27,026
Seriously.

1460
00:57:29,195 --> 00:57:30,363
What is this?

1461
00:57:30,947 --> 00:57:31,781
What is it?

1462
00:57:31,865 --> 00:57:33,032
It's not a guest, right?

1463
00:57:33,116 --> 00:57:34,534
IT'S THE LAST DAY

1464
00:57:34,617 --> 00:57:35,952
BUT NEW GUESTS?

1465
00:57:36,828 --> 00:57:37,829
What is this?

1466
00:57:38,997 --> 00:57:40,331
-It's a video call.
-A video call?

1467
00:57:42,959 --> 00:57:44,919
NERVOUS

1468
00:57:45,712 --> 00:57:47,130
Are you entering boot camp?

1469
00:57:47,213 --> 00:57:48,423
We're at the training center.

1470
00:57:48,506 --> 00:57:49,591
IT'S IN-BEOM AND JUN-YEOP

1471
00:57:51,050 --> 00:57:52,802
-It's In-beom.
-He's entering now.

1472
00:57:52,886 --> 00:57:54,345
12:50 P.M.

1473
00:57:54,429 --> 00:57:56,431
-The parade ground.
-I can't watch.

1474
00:57:56,514 --> 00:57:57,974
TIME LEFT UNTIL ENLISTMENT

1475
00:57:58,057 --> 00:57:59,225
Take care.

1476
00:57:59,309 --> 00:58:00,810
-Okay. Wish me luck.
-Okay.

1477
00:58:00,894 --> 00:58:02,395
I'll let you talk to everyone.

1478
00:58:02,479 --> 00:58:03,855
Hi.

1479
00:58:04,355 --> 00:58:05,523
-Hello.
-Hello.

1480
00:58:05,607 --> 00:58:07,525
Take care and stay healthy!

1481
00:58:07,609 --> 00:58:08,443
-Okay.
-Okay.

1482
00:58:08,526 --> 00:58:09,444
Now, Zuha.

1483
00:58:09,527 --> 00:58:10,653
They'll be so happy.

1484
00:58:10,737 --> 00:58:12,197
-Right.
-Hi.

1485
00:58:14,991 --> 00:58:16,117
-It's Kazuha.
-You can do it!

1486
00:58:16,201 --> 00:58:17,827
-Let's go, Kazuha!
-Let's go, Kazuha!

1487
00:58:17,911 --> 00:58:19,287
Hey, guys.

1488
00:58:20,705 --> 00:58:21,748
Good luck.

1489
00:58:21,831 --> 00:58:23,124
Take care.

1490
00:58:23,208 --> 00:58:24,876
-Thank you. Salute!
-Salute!

1491
00:58:24,959 --> 00:58:25,877
Salute.

1492
00:58:29,714 --> 00:58:31,799
What's it like in there?
Tougher than Kian's B&B?

1493
00:58:31,883 --> 00:58:33,635
Of course. Gosh.

1494
00:58:33,718 --> 00:58:36,262
Then, do they have to
wash up no matter what?

1495
00:58:36,346 --> 00:58:39,265
Is it mandatory?
Do they have to maintain personal hygiene?

1496
00:58:39,349 --> 00:58:40,475
Yeah, they have to.

1497
00:58:40,558 --> 00:58:42,060
What if you don't want to shower?

1498
00:58:42,143 --> 00:58:42,977
-You can't.
-No way.

1499
00:58:43,061 --> 00:58:45,104
I'm sure that's against military law.

1500
00:58:45,188 --> 00:58:47,357
So did you not learn properly
in the military?

1501
00:58:47,440 --> 00:58:48,900
You don't wash yourself often.

1502
00:58:50,652 --> 00:58:52,779
-I didn't see that coming at all.
-Right?

1503
00:58:52,862 --> 00:58:54,531
When I was in the military,

1504
00:58:54,614 --> 00:58:56,616
they kept telling me to shower.

1505
00:58:56,699 --> 00:58:59,994
And it did make me hate showering
after I was discharged.

1506
00:59:00,078 --> 00:59:02,163
I mean, it's always been a mystery to me.

1507
00:59:02,247 --> 00:59:04,958
"Why does he lie in bed
when he's covered in sweat?"

1508
00:59:05,041 --> 00:59:06,834
"Why is he putting
his head on the pillow?"

1509
00:59:06,918 --> 00:59:09,796
And when you tell me to wash up,

1510
00:59:09,879 --> 00:59:11,673
-it reminds me of that trauma.
-Really?

1511
00:59:11,756 --> 00:59:13,675
I think I was traumatized by you too.

1512
00:59:13,758 --> 00:59:16,010
Because of officers like you,

1513
00:59:16,094 --> 00:59:17,220
I became so defiant.

1514
00:59:17,303 --> 00:59:18,179
Really?

1515
00:59:18,263 --> 00:59:20,723
"Why do they keep telling me
to wash up? I won't!"

1516
00:59:20,807 --> 00:59:22,308
"I'll shower when I want to."

1517
00:59:22,392 --> 00:59:24,227
So you don't shower much these days?

1518
00:59:24,310 --> 00:59:27,063
No, I do shower,
but only when I want to.

1519
00:59:27,146 --> 00:59:28,731
CAN'T UNDERSTAND

1520
00:59:30,775 --> 00:59:32,151
The smell's not so bad yet.

1521
00:59:34,153 --> 00:59:37,991
Tonight's the last night.
Is there anything else you'd like to do?

1522
00:59:38,074 --> 00:59:40,535
How about we have dinner outside tonight?

1523
00:59:40,618 --> 00:59:41,703
-Outside?
-Yeah.

1524
00:59:41,786 --> 00:59:43,705
-I think it's a good idea.
-It'll be romantic.

1525
00:59:43,788 --> 00:59:45,582
-We'll make tables.
-We can sit on the snow.

1526
00:59:45,665 --> 00:59:47,834
How about we make tables with snow?

1527
00:59:47,917 --> 00:59:49,252
I think it'll be nice.

1528
00:59:49,335 --> 00:59:51,337
I'll try and design it.

1529
00:59:51,421 --> 00:59:52,755
Do you want to make a snowman?

1530
00:59:52,839 --> 00:59:54,507
BOSS'S IDEA
MAKE A SNOWMAN FOR DECORATION

1531
00:59:54,591 --> 00:59:55,425
Sounds good.

1532
00:59:55,508 --> 00:59:58,219
Make the snowman as big as you can.

1533
00:59:58,303 --> 01:00:00,054
Just make it as tall as me.

1534
01:00:00,138 --> 01:00:02,473
-Make it 192 cm tall. Yeah.
-192 cm tall?

1535
01:00:02,557 --> 01:00:05,476
It'll be nice
to do more things with the guests.

1536
01:00:07,562 --> 01:00:09,897
Like the campfires we had
when we were young,

1537
01:00:09,981 --> 01:00:11,649
we could light up some candles.

1538
01:00:11,733 --> 01:00:13,901
We always had that moment
during school trips.

1539
01:00:14,485 --> 01:00:15,820
Everyone would cry.

1540
01:00:15,903 --> 01:00:16,988
That sounds good.

1541
01:00:17,071 --> 01:00:20,325
It's because it'll feel different
to talk while holding candles.

1542
01:00:20,408 --> 01:00:21,826
Right, it'll be different.

1543
01:00:21,909 --> 01:00:24,203
-The candle thing sounds good.
-Yes.

1544
01:00:24,954 --> 01:00:26,581
-Let's go.
-Okay.

1545
01:00:26,664 --> 01:00:29,292
-Thank you for the food!
-Thank you for the food!

1546
01:00:29,375 --> 01:00:30,752
I wonder if they're having fun.

1547
01:00:30,835 --> 01:00:31,836
STAFF RETURNS AFTER LUNCH

1548
01:00:31,919 --> 01:00:33,171
KIAN'S B&B

1549
01:00:33,254 --> 01:00:34,339
CABLE CAR & SKYWALK

1550
01:00:34,422 --> 01:00:35,923
HYUN-SEO, SEONG-BHIN, YUN-WOO

1551
01:00:36,007 --> 01:00:36,841
Hello.

1552
01:00:36,924 --> 01:00:38,217
BALWANGSAN CABLE CAR

1553
01:00:39,802 --> 01:00:40,637
We're up so high.

1554
01:00:40,720 --> 01:00:42,764
-It's 1,458 m tall.
-That's impressive.

1555
01:00:42,847 --> 01:00:44,390
BALWANGSAN SUMMIT
ELEVATION OF 1,458 M

1556
01:00:44,474 --> 01:00:45,850
Elevation means "above sea level."

1557
01:00:45,933 --> 01:00:48,227
But sea levels are all different.

1558
01:00:48,311 --> 01:00:50,188
So it's mean sea level.

1559
01:00:50,271 --> 01:00:52,148
If the sea level rises
due to global warming,

1560
01:00:52,231 --> 01:00:53,232
its height would shrink?

1561
01:00:53,316 --> 01:00:54,150
That's right.

1562
01:00:54,233 --> 01:00:55,943
I hope the clouds pass by soon.

1563
01:00:56,444 --> 01:00:58,112
That's how clouds form.

1564
01:00:58,196 --> 01:00:59,489
Water vaporizes.

1565
01:00:59,572 --> 01:01:01,949
-As it rises, air pressure drops.
-The air expands.

1566
01:01:02,033 --> 01:01:03,868
It's fast, so adiabatic expansion happens.

1567
01:01:03,951 --> 01:01:05,536
According to thermodynamics,

1568
01:01:05,620 --> 01:01:08,164
the internal energy decreases,
causing a temperature drop.

1569
01:01:08,247 --> 01:01:10,500
AS ALTITUDE RISES,
SCIENCE TALK GROWS DEEPER

1570
01:01:10,583 --> 01:01:12,418
So how it works is…

1571
01:01:12,502 --> 01:01:13,628
SKY RANCH

1572
01:01:13,711 --> 01:01:15,213
SU-RYEON

1573
01:01:15,797 --> 01:01:17,715
It's snowing a lot.

1574
01:01:17,799 --> 01:01:18,633
YOUTUBER SU-RYEON

1575
01:01:18,716 --> 01:01:20,426
I'm at Sky Ranch now.

1576
01:01:20,510 --> 01:01:21,636
It's so pretty.

1577
01:01:21,719 --> 01:01:22,679
SKY RANCH

1578
01:01:25,848 --> 01:01:27,392
I love it!

1579
01:01:29,477 --> 01:01:31,479
I wonder if there are sheep out here.

1580
01:01:32,480 --> 01:01:33,690
FINDS A SHEEP TAKING A WALK

1581
01:01:33,773 --> 01:01:35,191
It's so cute.

1582
01:01:35,274 --> 01:01:36,484
What's its name?

1583
01:01:36,567 --> 01:01:37,527
It's Chanel.

1584
01:01:37,610 --> 01:01:38,444
Chanel?

1585
01:01:38,528 --> 01:01:39,696
Let's go, Chanel.

1586
01:01:39,779 --> 01:01:41,739
It's so excited.

1587
01:01:41,823 --> 01:01:44,450
You can give the hay and feed
to all the animals.

1588
01:01:44,534 --> 01:01:46,577
Thank you. Gosh, it's so cute.

1589
01:01:46,661 --> 01:01:48,246
It's Chanel's mukbang.

1590
01:01:48,913 --> 01:01:49,997
MEANWHILE, THE ICE CLIMBERS

1591
01:01:50,081 --> 01:01:50,915
Let's go.

1592
01:01:51,582 --> 01:01:53,251
But where do we go?

1593
01:01:54,544 --> 01:01:55,753
"Seonjaryeong Valley."

1594
01:01:55,837 --> 01:01:57,255
That's our destination.

1595
01:01:57,338 --> 01:01:59,006
IF YOU WALK UP 2 KM FROM SKY RANCH

1596
01:01:59,090 --> 01:02:00,216
BAEKDUDAEGAN SEONJARYEONG

1597
01:02:00,299 --> 01:02:01,926
ELEVATION OF 1,157 M
SEONJARYEONG VALLEY

1598
01:02:02,593 --> 01:02:03,636
Let's go. Follow me.

1599
01:02:03,720 --> 01:02:04,721
Is that the right way?

1600
01:02:04,804 --> 01:02:05,638
It is.

1601
01:02:06,514 --> 01:02:09,016
Right, when will we ever
get to see this much snow again?

1602
01:02:10,768 --> 01:02:11,978
The snow's so deep.

1603
01:02:12,061 --> 01:02:13,438
It's so heavy.

1604
01:02:13,521 --> 01:02:15,398
Hey, clear the path.

1605
01:02:16,399 --> 01:02:17,233
PLOWING THROUGH SNOW

1606
01:02:17,316 --> 01:02:18,276
This is a workout.

1607
01:02:18,359 --> 01:02:19,777
The horses are moving.

1608
01:02:20,903 --> 01:02:22,196
They're moving.

1609
01:02:24,532 --> 01:02:25,825
This is not easy.

1610
01:02:27,034 --> 01:02:28,494
It's getting tough.

1611
01:02:30,079 --> 01:02:31,080
Let's take a break.

1612
01:02:33,624 --> 01:02:34,751
I don't think I can make it.

1613
01:02:35,334 --> 01:02:36,836
GIVES UP GOING TO SEONJARYEONG

1614
01:02:38,546 --> 01:02:39,881
You even brought a pickax.

1615
01:02:39,964 --> 01:02:40,882
Shall we make it?

1616
01:02:40,965 --> 01:02:43,092
We're building our own house.

1617
01:02:43,718 --> 01:02:44,927
We'll do some shoveling.

1618
01:02:46,304 --> 01:02:47,764
It's more exciting than I thought.

1619
01:02:48,848 --> 01:02:49,766
It is.

1620
01:02:50,767 --> 01:02:52,059
How's this for a bar table?

1621
01:02:53,019 --> 01:02:53,936
HANGING MEDALS TOO

1622
01:02:54,520 --> 01:02:57,064
-It's already finished.
-It's our house now.

1623
01:02:57,982 --> 01:03:00,151
When will we get to play
like this in the snow again?

1624
01:03:00,651 --> 01:03:02,528
This is happiness. What else is there?

1625
01:03:03,154 --> 01:03:04,155
Thank you.

1626
01:03:04,238 --> 01:03:05,948
THE STAFF RETURN TO KIAN'S B&B

1627
01:03:06,032 --> 01:03:06,866
2:30 P.M.

1628
01:03:06,949 --> 01:03:08,409
It stopped snowing.

1629
01:03:09,076 --> 01:03:11,913
Kian, should we carve into the slope
and make chairs?

1630
01:03:11,996 --> 01:03:14,832
If we do it on flat ground,
it'll take forever.

1631
01:03:14,916 --> 01:03:16,501
The slope will be better.

1632
01:03:16,584 --> 01:03:18,377
We can just have them sit down this way.

1633
01:03:18,461 --> 01:03:19,337
HERE

1634
01:03:19,420 --> 01:03:20,797
We'll all have to do it together.

1635
01:03:20,880 --> 01:03:22,006
Okay, let's go.

1636
01:03:22,089 --> 01:03:22,924
Let's go.

1637
01:03:23,508 --> 01:03:24,801
Snow shovels.

1638
01:03:26,302 --> 01:03:27,136
The snow!

1639
01:03:27,220 --> 01:03:28,137
Hey.

1640
01:03:28,221 --> 01:03:29,806
KNEE-DEEP

1641
01:03:29,889 --> 01:03:30,723
Just this much.

1642
01:03:30,807 --> 01:03:32,058
Should we slide down?

1643
01:03:32,141 --> 01:03:33,935
GOING DOWN WHILE MAKING A PATH

1644
01:03:34,685 --> 01:03:36,354
AN ORDEAL FROM THE BEGINNING

1645
01:03:36,437 --> 01:03:37,605
Around here…

1646
01:03:38,272 --> 01:03:39,941
Let's make chairs here first.

1647
01:03:40,525 --> 01:03:42,360
Here? Facing which direction?

1648
01:03:42,443 --> 01:03:43,986
Facing that direction.

1649
01:03:44,070 --> 01:03:45,780
-Facing this way?
-That way.

1650
01:03:45,863 --> 01:03:48,616
VIEW OF KIAN'S B&B
IN THE MIDDLE OF SNOWY MOUNTAINS

1651
01:03:48,699 --> 01:03:50,159
-Here, right?
-Yeah. Dig here.

1652
01:03:50,243 --> 01:03:51,494
CONSTRUCTING OUTDOOR RESTAURANT

1653
01:03:51,577 --> 01:03:53,412
-Pile it up?
-Pile it up and make chairs.

1654
01:03:53,496 --> 01:03:54,580
Dex, should I not dig here?

1655
01:03:54,664 --> 01:03:57,250
Dig the front and place it in the back.

1656
01:03:57,333 --> 01:04:00,169
WHERE THE CHAIRS WILL BE MADE

1657
01:04:00,253 --> 01:04:01,379
Like this. Boom.

1658
01:04:01,462 --> 01:04:02,630
-Right.
-Bam!

1659
01:04:02,713 --> 01:04:04,048
PLACING AND FLATTENING THE SNOW

1660
01:04:04,131 --> 01:04:05,550
-Okay. Bam, bam.
-Bam, bam.

1661
01:04:05,633 --> 01:04:06,634
Let's do "bam, bam."

1662
01:04:06,717 --> 01:04:07,677
Like this. Bam, bam.

1663
01:04:07,760 --> 01:04:09,053
THEY BEGIN FLATTENING THE SNOW

1664
01:04:09,136 --> 01:04:10,847
-Zuha, it's "bam, bam."
-"Bam, bam"?

1665
01:04:22,191 --> 01:04:23,985
Zuha, have you ever done sapjil before?

1666
01:04:24,068 --> 01:04:25,361
"Sapsil"? What's that?

1667
01:04:25,444 --> 01:04:26,863
This. Have you done this before?

1668
01:04:26,946 --> 01:04:28,322
-No, never.
-Sap means "shovel."

1669
01:04:28,406 --> 01:04:30,449
-Sap means "shovel"?
-Yeah, that's right.

1670
01:04:30,533 --> 01:04:31,659
-Shovel, for sure?
-Right.

1671
01:04:31,742 --> 01:04:33,035
-Shovel, for sure.
-Okay.

1672
01:04:33,119 --> 01:04:34,120
That's right.

1673
01:04:34,203 --> 01:04:36,038
The work is endless at Kian's B&B.

1674
01:04:36,622 --> 01:04:37,707
Goodness.

1675
01:04:37,790 --> 01:04:39,417
It's not over until it's over.

1676
01:04:41,377 --> 01:04:42,545
I feel so hot.

1677
01:04:48,926 --> 01:04:50,595
See how it's hard over here?

1678
01:04:50,678 --> 01:04:51,512
If you sit on it…

1679
01:04:53,055 --> 01:04:54,265
-It's good.
-It's not bad.

1680
01:04:54,348 --> 01:04:55,308
COMFORTABLE

1681
01:04:55,391 --> 01:04:56,517
Let me take a seat too.

1682
01:04:57,393 --> 01:04:59,312
-It's not falling apart.
-Great.

1683
01:04:59,395 --> 01:05:00,521
I'm so comfortable here.

1684
01:05:00,605 --> 01:05:02,273
Right? That's your seat.

1685
01:05:02,356 --> 01:05:03,357
It's for your long legs.

1686
01:05:03,441 --> 01:05:04,609
MATS AS CUSHIONS TO FINISH UP

1687
01:05:04,692 --> 01:05:06,235
Let's lay down mats to sit on.

1688
01:05:06,319 --> 01:05:08,905
Yes, we need them
or our bottoms will be all wet.

1689
01:05:12,533 --> 01:05:13,367
This is awesome.

1690
01:05:13,451 --> 01:05:14,619
CHAIRS ARE COMPLETE

1691
01:05:16,454 --> 01:05:18,039
Let's make stairs.

1692
01:05:19,248 --> 01:05:20,708
STAIRS LEADING TO OUTDOOR RESTAURANT

1693
01:05:21,417 --> 01:05:23,002
Like a fancy restaurant.

1694
01:05:35,348 --> 01:05:37,391
Dex, did you just make stairs?

1695
01:05:37,475 --> 01:05:38,851
-Yes.
-Incredible.

1696
01:05:38,935 --> 01:05:39,769
STAIRS ARE COMPLETE

1697
01:05:39,852 --> 01:05:41,145
He knows what's needed.

1698
01:05:41,228 --> 01:05:42,980
How do I make a snowman?

1699
01:05:43,064 --> 01:05:44,273
ZUHA WANTS TO MAKE A SNOWMAN

1700
01:05:44,357 --> 01:05:46,150
I've never made a big one before.

1701
01:05:49,570 --> 01:05:50,863
What do I do?

1702
01:05:51,697 --> 01:05:55,034
SHE MAKES A PILE FIRST

1703
01:05:59,330 --> 01:06:02,667
A LARGE PILE

1704
01:06:07,505 --> 01:06:08,798
I'll help you.

1705
01:06:08,881 --> 01:06:10,925
Isn't the lower part big enough now?

1706
01:06:11,008 --> 01:06:12,134
I'll make it bigger.

1707
01:06:12,218 --> 01:06:13,302
Bigger?

1708
01:06:13,386 --> 01:06:14,428
As big as Yeon-koung.

1709
01:06:14,512 --> 01:06:16,347
A SNOWMAN AS TALL AS YEON-KOUNG

1710
01:06:20,309 --> 01:06:21,310
It's slowly…

1711
01:06:22,019 --> 01:06:23,187
It's slowly getting bigger.

1712
01:06:23,270 --> 01:06:24,772
How big should it be?

1713
01:06:24,855 --> 01:06:26,857
IT'S AS TALL AS THE BOSS NOW

1714
01:06:26,941 --> 01:06:29,276
It's big. It's so big.

1715
01:06:29,360 --> 01:06:31,654
Hold on. Can I lift this?

1716
01:06:31,737 --> 01:06:35,241
A BIG SNOWBALL?

1717
01:06:36,117 --> 01:06:37,368
Move over a bit.

1718
01:06:46,002 --> 01:06:47,420
One more.

1719
01:06:49,588 --> 01:06:51,090
I can get this up there, right?

1720
01:06:56,554 --> 01:06:57,888
Geez! Damn it.

1721
01:06:57,972 --> 01:06:59,515
KIAN'S BIZARRE B&B SEASON 2

1722
01:07:47,271 --> 01:07:49,273
Subtitle translation by: Wayne Ryu
